[Corollary cor:optimal of arXiv:2606.24465, 'History estimation in random recursive trees:\\Pointwise approach via iterated Jordan cent'] For each $\alpha>0$, there exists a constant $c_\alpha$ such that for any label-invariant estimator $\widehat{\sigma}$, and any $n\ge 2$,
    \begin{equation*}
        R_{\alpha}(\widehat{\sigma}) \ge 
        \begin{dcases}
            c_\alpha n^{2-\alpha}, &\text{if }\alpha\in(0,2),\\
            c_\alpha\log n,&\text{if }\alpha=2, \\
            c_\alpha,&\text{if }\alpha>2.
        \end{dcases}
    \end{equation*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 33 of arXiv:2608.29872, 'Local Laws and Outlier Eigenvalues for Spiked Separable Covariance Matrices'] If $x\ne 0$ is not an eigenvalue of $\mathcal Q_1$, then it is an eigenvalue of $\widetilde{\mathcal Q}_1$ if and only if
\begin{equation}
\det\left(\mathcal{D}^{-1}+x \mathbf U^* G(x) \mathbf U\right)=0.
\end{equation}

