[Lemma lem:11 of arXiv:2512.09219, 'Strong confluence of geodesics in Liouville quantum gravity'] Fix $z\in \mathbb{C}, r>0$. On the event $F_r(z)$, the following hold.
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item  Any path $\xi\subseteq B_{\delta_2 r}(V_r(z))$ from $B_{\delta_2 r}(I_u)$ to $B_{\delta_2 r}( (\mathcal{M}\setminus S_u)\cup S_v\cup \mathcal{A}_{v_+}\cup \mathcal{A}_{v_-})$ must necessarily intersect $B_{\delta_2 r}(\mathcal{A}_{u_-}\cup \mathcal{A}_{u_+})$.
  \item Any path $\xi\subseteq B_{\delta_2 r}(V_r(z))$ from $B_{\delta_2 r}(I_v)$ to $B_{\delta_2 r}( (\mathcal{M}\setminus S_v)\cup S_u\cup \mathcal{A}_{u_+}\cup \mathcal{A}_{u_-})$ must necessarily intersect $B_{\delta_2 r}(\mathcal{A}_{v_-}\cup \mathcal{A}_{v_+})$.
  \end{enumerate}

[Mylem 8 (Corollary 1.4 in \cite{RV_imrn}) of arXiv:2607.00495, 'Rank deficiency of Bernoulli random matrices for growing corank'] Consider a random vector $X = (X_1,...,X_n)$ where $X_i$ are real-valued independent random variables. Let $t, b \ge  0$ be such that
\begin{align*}
    \mathcal{L}\left( X_{i}, t \right) \le b \text{ for all } i \in [n]
\end{align*}
 Let $P$ be an orthogonal projection in $\mathbb{R}^{n}$ onto a $d$-dimensional subspace. Then
 \begin{align*}
     \mathcal{L}\left( PX, t\sqrt{d}  \right) \le \left( C_{\ref{Small ball probability for linear image}}b \right)^{d},
 \end{align*}
 where $C_{\ref{Small ball probability for linear image}}>0$ is a absolute constant. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

