{"artifact_digest":"sha256:9b277e686fef5e819284ab31777d1fc0aa66356b72da5bdd4856420a006ef438","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/9b/9b277e686fef5e819284ab31777d1fc0aa66356b72da5bdd4856420a006ef438.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:df9b54fdab990326dedde7f455a4e2d3f634665791404cd8b2dd6cbaf71d5e9e","bundle_entry_key":"2606-08325-lemma-20-asympdfold","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_107","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_107.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2606-08325-lemma-20-asympdfold","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Let us abbreviate $ \alpha := (d-1)/d<1$ such that  \(p_n\sim Cn^{-\alpha}\). A simple 
			Riemann-sum estimate gives
			\[
			\begin{aligned}
				U_k(N)
				&=
				C^k
				\sum_{\substack{i_1,\ldots,i_k\ge1\\ i_1+\cdots+i_k=N}}
				i_1^{-\alpha}\cdots i_k^{-\alpha}
				(1+o(1))                                                  \\
				&\sim
				C^k N^{k-1-k\alpha}
				\int_{\substack{x_j>0\\ x_1+\cdots+x_k=1}}
				x_1^{-\alpha}\cdots x_k^{-\alpha}\,d\sigma(x),
			\end{aligned}
			\]
