[Prop branching-rules of arXiv:2510.23430, 'On the Martin boundary for discrete TASEP'] There exist symmetric functions $G^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda/\mu}\in\hat\Lambda$, $g^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda/\mu}\in\Lambda$ satisfying the following properties:
\begin{itemize}
\item One variable specializations $G^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda/\mu}(x), g^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda/\mu}(x)$ coincide with (equation Gone of the paper), (equation gone of the paper);

\item $G^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda/\varnothing}=G^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda}$, $g^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda/\varnothing}=g^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda}$;

\item The following branching rules hold for any sets of variables $\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{y}$
$$
G_{\lambda/\mu}^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}(\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{y})=\sum_{\nu}G^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda/\nu}(\mathbf{x})G^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\nu/\mu}(\mathbf{y}),
$$
$$
g_{\lambda/\mu}^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}(\mathbf{x}, \mathbf{y})=\sum_{\nu}g^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\lambda/\nu}(\mathbf{x})g^{(\mathfrak a,\mathfrak b)}_{\nu/\mu}(\mathbf{y}),
$$
\end{itemize}

[Definition 25 of arXiv:2607.29495, 'Fast Mixing for Low-Temperature Potts Models via Poisson Trees'] Let $\ell$ be a positive integer and
let $T\sim \cT$.  For every vertex $v\in V(T)$, 
let $T_{v,\ell}$ be the maximal subtree of~$T_v$ in which each root-to-leaf path contains at most $\ell$ good vertices, excluding the root~$v$.

[Lemma lem:first-chaosn of arXiv:2411.10419, 'Lower bounds on the top Lyapunov exponent for linear PDEs driven by the 2D stochastic Navi'] Consider the map $ \Phi $ as in (equation e:def-phi of the paper) with $ L [u] = u \cdot \nabla
$.  For any $ 1 <\alpha < \beta < \mathbf{a}/2 $, we can estimate uniformly
over $ \kappa \in (0, 1] $:
\begin{equs}
\mathbb{E} \bigl\| \mathcal{L}_{1}  \bigl[  \Phi \bigl[ \widetilde{X},
\Phi[ X^{0}, Y] \bigr]_{t_{\star}^{\kappa} (M)}+ \Phi \bigl[ X^{0}, \Phi[ \widetilde{X}, Y]
\bigr]_{t_{\star}^{\kappa} (M)} \bigr] \bigr\|^{2}\lesssim (t_{\star}^{\kappa} (M))^{4} \kappa^{-1} \| u_{0}
\|^{2}_{\mathcal{C}^{\beta}} \| \varrho_{0} \|_{H^{- \alpha}}^{2} \;.
\end{equs}

