[Lem func-vanish of arXiv:2601.19145, 'Stochastic Persistence in Infinite Dimensions'] Assume (fass1 of the paper), (fass2 of the paper) and define
    \begin{equation}
        H(\phi) \coloneqq \sum_{i=1}^n \rho_iH_i(\phi) \,,
    \end{equation}
   where for any $\phi \in \mathcal{M}$
   \begin{equation}
   H_i(\phi) = 
   \begin{cases}
   -f_i(\phi) + \frac{1}{2}\sigma_{ii}g_i^2(\phi) & \textrm{if }  x_i = \phi_i(0) =0 \\        
   V_i'(x_i)x_if_i(\phi) + \frac{1}{2}\sigma_{ii}^2V_i''(x_i)x_i^2g_i^2(\phi) & \textrm{otherwise} \,,
       \end{cases}
   \end{equation}
and $V$ is defined in (fass1-and-fass2-are-satisfied of the paper). Then
(as-V of the paper)(as-vanish of the paper) is satisfied with the measure $\mu + \delta_0$ and $W', V$, where $\mu$ is defined in (fass1 of the paper) and $W'$ and $V$
 are as in (func-WU of the paper) and (fass1-and-fass2-are-satisfied of the paper) respectively.

[Proposition p:V adapted of arXiv:2411.04773, 'Meeting of squared Bessel flow lines and application to the skew Brownian motion'] (i) Almost surely, for any $r\ge 0$: for any $x \in [V(-r),z)$
    \begin{equation}
        \widehat{\mathcal S}_{x,z}\circ \mathcal S_{-r,x}(0) >0.
    \end{equation}
    while for any $x\in [-r,V(-r))$, 
    \begin{equation}
         \widehat{\mathcal S}_{x,z} \circ\mathcal S_{-r,x}(0)=0.
    \end{equation}
    In particular,  with the convention that $\inf \emptyset=+\infty$, (see Figure (fig:meeting3pr of the paper))
    \begin{equation}
        V(-r)=\inf \{x\in[-r,z): \widehat {\mathcal S}_{x,z}\circ\mathcal S_{-r,x}(0)>0 \} \land z.
    \end{equation}

(ii)    For any $r\ge 0$, $V(-r)$ is measurable with respect to $\mathscr W^*_r$.

[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2605.14254, '2605.14254'] The process $\zeta^{\lambda,z}$ is a Feller process, that is, its semigroup $Q^{\lambda,z}$ satisfies the following statements:
		\begin{enumerate}
			\item[(i)] $Q^{\lambda,z}_t h(y) \rightarrow h(y)$ as $t \rightarrow 0, h \in C_0(\{0,1\}\times \mathbb{R}), y=(y_1, y_2) \in \{0,1\}\times \mathbb{R}$
			\item[(ii)] $ Q^{\lambda,z}_t C_0(\{0,1\}\times \mathbb{R}) \subset C_0(\{0,1\}\times \mathbb{R}), t \geq 0$.
		\end{enumerate}

