[Lemma lem:ancientbis of arXiv:2608.20537, 'Persistent anisotropy in multi-dimensional\\ branching Brownian motion'] The function $\bar h_T(t,x)$ from (equation 26apr2310 of the paper) is the minimal positive solution to the global-in-time backward problem
  \begin{equation}

    \begin{cases}
      \partial_t\bar h_T+\Delta \bar h_T+\bar h_T-\bar h_T^2=0, & t\in\mathbb{R}, x\in\mathcal{A}^\mathrm{c}(t),\\
      \bar h_T(t,x)=1, & t>T, x\in\mathcal{A}(t).
    \end{cases}
  \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:2s5c-ssc-low of arXiv:2411.00930, '\bf \Large Asymptotic Product-form Steady-state for Multiclass Queueing Networks: A Reentr'] For any fixed $\eta\in\mathbb{R}_-^5$,
    \begin{align*}
        &\lim_{r\to0}\phi^{(r)}(0,0,0,r^2\eta_4,0)-\phi^{(r)}(r^2\eta_1,0,0,r^2\eta_4,0)=0,\\
        &\lim_{r\to0}\phi_k^{(r)}(0,0,0,r^2\eta_4,0)-\phi_k^{(r)}(r^2\eta_1,0,0,r^2\eta_4,0)=0,\quad k\in\{1,\ldots,5\}.
    \end{align*}

