body:
[Lemma E[multi_edges]_asymp of arXiv:2604.05921, 'Simplicity of random hypergraphs'] If $\forall e \in E: \delta_e = \delta\in O(1)$ and 
\begin{enumerate}
    \item $\mathds{E}[d_U^{2\delta}] \in o(n)$
    \item $\exists c > 0: \lim_{n \rightarrow \infty} \mathds{P}(d_U \geq 2 \delta) \geq c$ 
\end{enumerate}
then
\begin{align*}
    \mathds{E}[M_n] = \frac{(\delta-1)!}{2\delta}  (n \mathds{E}[d_U])^2 \Bigg(\frac{\mathds{E}[d_U^2] - \mathds{E}[d_U]}{n\mathds{E}[d_U]^2}\Bigg)^{\delta} (1+o(1)).
\end{align*} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

