[Definition of arXiv:2608.30346, '\textbf{Classification complexity of homeomorphism group actions}'] Let \(G\) be a Polish group acting continuously on a Polish space \(X\). The action of \(G\) on \(X\) is \textit{turbulent} if
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item[(T1)] every orbit is meager,
        \item[(T2)] every orbit is dense, and
        \item[(T3)] every local orbit is somewhere dense, that is for any open \(U \subset X\), \( x \in U\) and open \(1_G \in V \subset G\), \(\mathcal{O}(x,U,V)\) is somewhere dense.
    \end{enumerate}

[Prop series of arXiv:2604.14122, 'The scaling limit of random walk and\\ the intrinsic metric on planar critical percolation'] Let $V\in\mathfrak{C}$ and let $x,y,z\in \mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V}$ such that $z$ separates $x$ from $y$ in $\mathcal{X}\cap\overline{V}$. Then
\begin{equation}
    \mathfrak{d}_V(x,y)=\mathfrak{d}_V(x,z)+\mathfrak{d}_V(z,y).
\end{equation}

