[Theorem theo:minimaxgan of arXiv:2411.10235, '\textbf{Smooth transport map via diffusion process}'] Let $n\in \mathbb{N}_{>0}$, $\beta> 0$, $p^\star \in \mathcal{F}_\beta$ and $(X_1,...,X_n)$ an i.i.d. sample of law $p^\star$. The GAN estimator $\hat{g}$ (equation eq:gan of the paper) using the classes of functions $\mathcal{G}$ (equation eq:G of the paper) and $\mathcal{D}$ (equation eq:D of the paper), satisfies for all $\gamma>0$
\begin{align*}
    \sup_{p^\star \in \mathcal{F}_\beta}\ \mathbb{E}_{X_i}[d_{\mathcal{H}^{\gamma}_1}(\hat{g}_{\# }\gamma_d,p^\star)] =\tilde{O}\left( \inf_{\hat{\theta}\in \Theta}\ \sup_{p^\star\in \mathcal{F}_\beta}\ \mathbb{E}_{X_i}[d_{\mathcal{H}^{\gamma}_1}(\hat{\theta},p^\star)]\right),
\end{align*}
where $\Theta$ denotes the set of all possible estimators  of $p^\star$ based on n sample.

