			$$ 	X^k=\sum_{M\geq k} B_M^{(k)}2^{-M}$$
			with 
			\[ B_M^{(k)} =
			\sum_{\substack{i_1,\ldots,i_k\ge1\\
					i_1+\cdots+i_k=M}} \xi_{i_1}\cdots\xi_{i_k}
			\]
			for $1 \leq k \leq d$. Note that is just a binomial expansion and in particular $B_M^{(k)}$ does not need to coincide with the binary digits. 
			We still have modulo \(1\),
			\begin{equation}
			2^NQ(X)\equiv \sum_{\ell\ge1}2^{-\ell} \sum_{k=1}^{d} a_k B_{N+\ell}^{(k)}
			\pmod 1,
