The left side is $\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(\mathbf X^\circ)}{i}\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(\mathbf X^\circ)}{j}$ after translating the initial point to zero, and the two integrals sum to $\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(\mathbf X^\circ)}{ij+ji}=\inner{\mathrm{Sig}(\mathbf X^\circ)}{i\mathbin{\sqcup\!\sqcup} j}$. For a finite-variation jump path this is exactly (prop:ito-defect of the paper); for a continuous semimartingale it is the usual It\^o{}--Stratonovich correction.

