body:
[Proposition thm:characterization of arXiv:2604.22453, 'Adapted Wasserstein Barycenters of Gaussian Processes'] Let $
\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
$ be a minimizer of (equation eq:restricted.ABW.factor.problem of the paper).  Then there exist Procrustes optimizers
\[
Q^k\in\mathscr Q(
\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
,L^k):=\argmin_{Q\in\mathscr O(T,d)}\|
\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
-L^kQ\|_F^2,
\qquad k=1,\ldots,K,
\]
such that
\begin{equation}

\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
=\sum_{k=1}^K\lambda_kL^kQ^k.
\end{equation}
Conversely, if $
\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
$ and $(Q^1,\ldots,Q^K)$ solve the joint global minimization problem
\[
\inf_{L\in\mathscr L(T,d),\,Q^1,\ldots,Q^K\in\mathscr O(T,d)}
\sum_{k=1}^K\lambda_k\|L-L^kQ^k\|_F^2,
\]
with each $Q^k\in\mathscr Q(
\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
,L^k)$, then $
\accentset{\overline{\hphantom{L}}}{L}
$ is a restricted minimizer.

