body:
[Lemma l:exactcov of arXiv:2411.08848, 'Stationary random measures: Covariance asymptotics, variance bounds and central limit theo'] Let ${\mathcal X}$ be a stationary random measure on $\mathbb{R}^d$ and let $f,g:\mathbb{R}^d\to \mathbb{R}$. Assume that
\begin{enumerate}
\item  $\int |z|^m |{\bf K}|(\mathrm{d} z) < \infty$ for all  $m\ge 0$.
\item $g$ is real analytic. Further, $f,g$ and   partial derivatives of $g$ of all orders are in $L^1\cap L^2$.
\item $\sum\limits_{\gamma\in \mathbb{Z}_+^d}\frac{1}{\gamma!}\|\partial^{\gamma}g\|_2\int |z^{\gamma}| \ |{\bf K}| (\mathrm{d} z) < \infty$.
\end{enumerate}
Let $ I(\gamma):=\int z^{\gamma} {\bf K}(\mathrm{d} z)$ for $\gamma\in \mathbb{Z}_+^d$.   Then

\begin{equation}

 \mathrm{Cov}({\mathcal X}(f),{\mathcal X}(g))  = \sum_{p\ge 0}Q_{2p}^{{\bf K}}(f,g),
 \end{equation}
 where 
 \begin{align} 
 Q_m^{{\bf K}}(f,g)=\begin{cases}
 (\lambda_D + I(0))\ \langle f,g\rangle  &\mbox{ if }m=0, \\
 \sum\limits_{\gamma \in \mathbb{Z}^d_+:\ |\gamma|=m}\frac{1}{\gamma!}I(\gamma)\langle f,  \partial^{\gamma}g \rangle &\mbox{ if }m\ge 1.
 \end{cases}
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

