\(\mathcal E_{rm}(x+y)\). By (equation eq:E-commutator of the paper), its coefficient on the left-hand side is
\begin{align*}
  &\mathcal S(ry)^b
  \sum_{k\ge0}
  \frac{(x\mathcal S(rx))^k(y\mathcal S(ry))^{m-k}}
  {k!(1+b)_{m-k}}
  \varsigma\bigl(r(ky-(m-k)x)\bigr).
\end{align*}
Using
\begin{equation}
  \frac{(1+b)_m}{(1+b)_{m-k}}=k!\binom{m+b}{k},  
\end{equation}
this coefficient becomes
\[
  \frac{\mathcal S(ry)^b(y\mathcal S(ry))^m}{(1+b)_m}
  \sum_{k\geq0}
  \binom{m+b}{k}
  \left(\frac{\varsigma(rx)}{\varsigma(ry)}\right)^k
  \varsigma\bigl(r(ky-(m-k)x)\bigr).
\]
The elementary binomial identity
