[Definition eq:face-integral of arXiv:2609.01825, 'On everywhere locally soluble varieties \\ in families over toric bases'] We say that a vector $\vec\ell\in \mathbb{R}^s$ is \emph{of convergent type} for the face $\cal F$ if the integral
\begin{equation}
	\int_{\cal F} \prod_{i=1}^s t_i^{\ell_i} d \mu,
\end{equation}
where $d\mu$ stands for the $d$-dimensional Lebesgue measure on the face $\cal F$,
is finite.

