[Definition definition-property-star of arXiv:2609.00794, 'On operators whose adjoints or second adjoints attain their norms'] Let $X$ and $Y$ be Banach spaces. The pair $(X,Y)$ is said to have \textit{property $(P^\star)$} if there is a relatively $\operatorname{WOT}$ compact set $K \subseteq \mathcal{L}_{w^*, w^*}(Y^*, X^*)$ such that 
\begin{equation*}
0 \in \overline{K}^{\operatorname{WOT}} \ \ \ \mbox{and} \ \ \ 0 \not\in \overline{\co}^{\|\cdot\|}(K).
\end{equation*}

