[Lemma l:B-preimage of arXiv:2411.12003, 'Central Limit Theorem for non-stationary random products of $\SL(2, \R)$ matrices'] For any $B\in {\mathrm{SL}}(2,{\mathbb R})$ for at least one of two coordinate vectors $e_j$ one has
\begin{equation}
{\rm dist}(f_{B}^{-1}[e_j],\mathbf{r}(B)) \le \frac{1}{\|B\|^2}.
\end{equation}

