[Corollary 33 of arXiv:2606.09904, 'Non-explosion principles for branched rough differential equations with unbounded coeffici'] For any \(f \in \CF_{N - 1}\) and \(n \le N - |f|\), we have that 
  \begin{equation}
    \|D^n \partial^f_X \phi(Y)\|_{\infty; I_r} \lesssim l(r)^{(1 - n)\alpha + \delta}
  \end{equation}
  for any \(r, \delta > 0\). Moreover, in the special case where \(n = 1\), we have that 
  \begin{equation}
    \|D\partial^f_X \phi(Y)\|_{\infty; I_r} \lesssim (\log l(r))^{\gamma \Lambda_1([f])}. 
  \end{equation}

