body:
[Lemma lem:gauge_change_loop of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a finite bipartite graph. The weight function $\mathbf w : E\to \mathbb{R}$ is gauge equivalent to the uniform weight function if and only if for every loop $\gamma$ of $G$, we have 
    \begin{align}
        w_{e_1}w_{e_3}\dots w_{e_{2k-1}} = w_{e_2} w_{e_4}\dots w_{e_{2k}}
    \end{align}
    where $e_1,\dots, e_{2k}$ are the edges around $\gamma$.

