[Lemma 2-l09 of arXiv:2412.04015, 'Linear fluctuation of interfaces in Glauber-Kawasaki dynamics'] There exists a finite constant ${\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)$, depending
only on ${\boldsymbol u}^N$, $A$, the dimension $d$ and uniformly bounded in
$N$, such that
\begin{equation*}
\int  |\, {\mathcal W}^{(1)}_\ell\,| \, f\; d\nu^N \; \le\;
{\mathfrak c}({\boldsymbol u}^N)\, \Vert G\Vert_\infty \,
\big\{ H_N(f) \,+\, (N/\ell)^d\, \big\} 
\end{equation*}
for all density $f$ with respect to $\nu^N$ and $N> 4\ell$.

