[Proposition 15 (Exponential law of large numbers for the Stein velocity) of arXiv:2608.28827, 'Quantitative Target Convergence and Uniform-in-Time\\ Propagation of Chaos for Langevin-Re'] Under Assumptions~\ref{ass:core-target} and \ref{ass:concentration}, together with either kernel assumption, there are $\lambda>0$ and $1\le C_G<\infty$, independent of $N$ and $t$, such that
\begin{equation}
    \int e^{\lambda G_t^N}\,d\mu_t^{\otimes N}\le C_G.
\end{equation}

