[Definition def:VDC of arXiv:2609.04045, 'Heat content and spectrum for subordinated sub-Laplacians'] An open set $\Omega\subset\mathbb{G}$ is said to satisfy the \emph{volume density condition} if there exists $c>0$ such that for all $r>0$ and $x\in\partial\Omega$,
    \begin{align*}
        \operatorname{Vol}(\overline{\Omega}^c\cap \mathbb{B}(x,r))\geqslant c r^Q,
    \end{align*}
    where $Q$ is the homogeneous dimension of $\mathbb{G}$.

