[Corollary of arXiv:2412.06420, 'Accuracy, Estimates, and Representation Results'] For $p$ probabilistic with $\mathrm{Exp}_p[V]=e$, 
		\begin{align}
		\mathrm{Exp}_p\mathsf{acc}(e)-\mathrm{Exp}_p\mathsf{acc}(x)&=\int_x^e(e-t)m(t)\dd{t}
		\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2512.08595, 'Small time asymptotics of spectral heat content of isotropic processes'] For any nonnegative measurable function $f$ on $\R^d$ one has
		\begin{align*}
			Q^X_f(t)=\int_{\R^d}\E_x\left[\inf_{0\le s\le t} f(X_s)\right]dx.
		\end{align*}
		In particular, $Q^X_{\mathbbm{1}_\Omega}(t)=Q^X_\Omega(t)$ for any open set $\Omega$.

