[Theorem 21 of arXiv:2606.21111, 'On Elephant Random Walk with Delayed Amnesia'] Let $(4a-1)/4a<p\le 1$. Then,
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\frac{S_n}{n^{2a(p-1)+1}}=L \ \ \text{a.s.,}
\end{equation}
where $L$ is some non-degenerate random variable. Also, we have the following mean square convergence:
\begin{equation}
\lim_{n\to\infty}\mathbb{E}\Big(\Big|\frac{S_n}{n^{2a(p-1)+1}}-L\Big|^2\Big)=0.
\end{equation}

