[Lemma lem:12 of arXiv:2512.09219, 'Strong confluence of geodesics in Liouville quantum gravity'] Suppose that (equation it:geodstar of the paper) in Lemma (lem:geodesic_between_geodesics of the paper) holds. We then have the following:
  \begin{enumerate}
  \item For any $0\leq \alpha<\beta\leq \ell(\sigma_\eta^*;D_h)$ such that $\sigma_\eta^*\lvert_{[\alpha,\beta]}\subseteq \overline{V_\eta}$ and $\beta-\alpha \geq (25d_H^1(\eta_*,\eta))^{\chi/\chi'}$, the path $\sigma_\eta^*\lvert_{[\alpha,\beta]}$ must intersect $\xi_\eta^{l_1},\xi_\eta^{l_2}$ for some $l_1,l_2\in [T_*/10,T-T_*/10]$ satisfying $l_2-l_1\geq 4d_H^1(\eta_*,\eta)$
  \item  For any $0\leq \alpha<\beta\leq \ell(\sigma_\eta^*;D_h)$ such that $\sigma_\eta^*\lvert_{[\alpha,\beta]}\subseteq W_{T_*/10+3d_H^1(\eta_*,\eta),T-T_*/10-3d_H^1(\eta_*,\eta)}$ and $\beta-\alpha \geq (25K\varepsilon_{k_\eta})^{\chi/\chi'}$, the path $\sigma_\eta^*\lvert_{[\alpha,\beta]}$ must intersect $\xi_\eta^{l_1},\xi_\eta^{l_2}$ for some $l_1,l_2\in [T_*/10+3d_H^1(\eta_*,\eta),T-T_*/10-3d_H^1(\eta_*,\eta)]$ satisfying $l_2-l_1\geq 4K\varepsilon_{k_\eta}$.
  \end{enumerate}

