[Theorem 178 of arXiv:2605.03236, 'Stochastic It\^o Equations and Parabolic Second-Order Equations with singular Drift'] Suppose that \eqref{12.10,1} is satisfied
with an integer $n >d/4$ and $\lambda=0 $. Let $f\in C^{\infty}_{0}$. Then 
\begin{equation}

 \sum_{n=1}^{\infty}\int_{\Gamma_{n}(t_{0})}T_{0,t_{n }}
Q_{t_{n},...,t_{0}}f(x_{0})\,d t_{n } \cdot...\cdot d t_{1}\leq
N\Big(\int_{\bR^{d}}|Df|^{4n}\,dx\Big)^{1/(2n)},
\end{equation}
where $N$ depends only on $d,\delta,p_{0},\rho_{0},n,t_{0}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 17 of arXiv:2606.27774, 'Variational Formulas for the Spectrum of\\ Block Wishart Matrices'] For $\bS\in\bbH_+^k$ and $\bT\in \sa{k}{\C}$,
     $\bS$ is invertible and satisfies
    \begin{equation}

    \|\bS^{-1}\|_\op \le \|\Im(\bS)^{-1}\|_\op,\quad\quad \Im(\bS^{-1}) = -\bS^{-1}\Im(\bS)\bS^{*-1}\prec\bzero.
    \end{equation}

