[Thm legendre_duality of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix $\Lambda$. Then $\sigma(s)$ is the Legendre dual of $F(\alpha)$, i.e. for all $s\in \mathcal{N}(\Lambda)$, 
    \begin{equation}
        \sigma(s) = \max_{\alpha=(\alpha_1,\dots,\alpha_d)\in \mathbb{R}^d} - F(\alpha) + \sum_{i=1}^d s_i \alpha_i.
    \end{equation}

