[Definition 40 of arXiv:2607.18104, '2607.18104'] Let $\hfixp_0 \in \UCp$ and $\Lp$ be a periodic directed landscape on $(\mathbb{T} \times \R)^{2}_{\uparrow}$. Then define the random function $(y,t) \mapsto \hfixp(\hfixp_0;y,t)$ for all $y\in \mathbb{T}$ and $t >0$ by
\begin{equation}
 \hfixp\big(\hfixp_0;y,t\big) := \sup_{x\in \mathbb{T}} \big( \hfixp_0(x) + \Lp(x,0;y,t)\big).
\end{equation}

[Proposition prop:autocorrelation of arXiv:2507.16188, 'The noisy voter model with general initial conditions'] Let $G=(V,E)$ be a connected graph on $n$ vertices. Fix an initial state $\mathsf{x}_0 \in \mathfrak{C}_q^{V}$. Let $\psi_1,\ldots,\psi_{n}$ be an $L^2(\pi_G)$-orthonormal basis of eigenfunctions of the transition matrix $P$ of the discrete-time simple random walk on~$G$, and let $\lambda_1,\ldots,\lambda_{n}$ be their corresponding eigenvalues. Further define
\begin{equation} \gamma_l = 1-(1-\theta)\lambda_l
\qquad\mbox{for $l=1,\ldots,n$}\,.
\end{equation}
Then, for every $t>0$,
\begin{align}
\mathcal{A}^{(2)}_t(\mathsf{x}_0) = \frac1q \sum_{k=1}^{q-1} \sum_{v \in V} \pi_G(v)\big|\mathbb{E}_{\mathsf{x}_0}[X_t(v)^k]\big|^2
&= \frac1q \sum_{k=1}^{q-1} \sum_{l=1}^{n} |\langle \mathsf{x}_0^k, \psi_l\rangle_{\pi_G}|^2 e^{-2 \gamma_l t}\,.

\end{align}
Consequently, for any $s \geq 0$, we have
\begin{align}
e^{-(4-2\theta)s}  \leq &\frac{\mathcal{A}^{(2)}_{t+s}(\mathsf{x}_0)}{\mathcal{A}^{(2)}_t(\mathsf{x}_0)} \leq e^{-2\theta s} \,,
\end{align}
and in particular $\frac{q-1}q e^{-(4-2\theta)t} \leq \mathcal{A}^{(2)}_t (\mathsf{x}_0) \leq \frac{q-1}q e^{-2\theta t}$.

