prove that for any $\alpha\in\mathbb F_{q^2}$, the equation
$$x+\gamma {\rm Tr}_{q}^{q^2} (c_1 x+ c_2 x^2+c_3 x^3+x^{q+2})=\alpha$$
has a unique solution in $\mathbb F_{q^2}$. Substitute $x=\alpha+\gamma u$, $u\in\mathbb F_q$,
in $f_1(x)=\alpha$; we get the following cubic in the variable $u$
\begin{equation}
  A\,u^3+B(\alpha)\,u^2+C(\alpha)\,u+D(\alpha)=0,
\end{equation}
where, for $y\in\mathbb F_{q^2}$,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
