body:
[Teo 12 of arXiv:2608.02103, '$p$-Adic Diffusion and Random Walks on $[0,1]$'] Let \(X_t\in [0,1]\) be the strong Markov process attached to the infinitesimal generator \(D_f\) with probability transition \(p_t(x,\cdot)\). Let \(P_f\) be the operator defined on \(L^2(\mathbb{Z}_p,\mu)\) defined by equation (\ref{eq:padicoperator}). Let \(X^{*}_t:=\rho^{-1}(X_t)\) be the pull-back of \(X_t\). 
    Then the following holds
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item The attached semigroups are unitarily equivalent:
        \begin{equation*}
            e^{tD_f}=\rho^{*-1} e^{tP_f}\rho^{*}
        \end{equation*}
        \item The pull-back \(X^{*}_t\in \mathbb{Z}_p\) is a strong Markov process on \(\mathbb{Z}_p\) with probability transition \(p_t^{*}(y,\cdot)\) satisfying
        \[p_t^{*}(x,B)=p_t(\rho(x),\rho(B)),\]for any Borel set \(B\subset \mathbb{Z}_p\).
    \end{enumerate}

