[Defi of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] For  $\mathsf{P}_i\in \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$ we denote by $ \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)$ the set of all $\sigma$-finite stationary  (with respect to the shifts $(\theta_x)_{x\in \IR^2}$) measures  $ \mathsf{Q}$ on $\Gamma_{\IR^2}$ such that:
    \begin{itemize}
        \item[i)] The Palm measure $ \mathsf{Q}^0$ of $ \mathsf{Q}$  is a probability measure and $(\mathrm{Pr}^{\Gamma}_i)_{\#} \mathsf{Q}^0=\mathsf{P}_i^0$ for $i=0,1$.
        \item[ii)]  The measure $ \mathsf{Q}$ is concentrated on the set of monotone configurations $\bar\xi\in \Gamma_{\IR^2}$.
    \end{itemize}

[Theorem thm:S-Z-liouville of arXiv:2608.11931, '\texorpdfstring{Nonlinear parabolic characterizations of stochastic completeness at infini'] Assume $\kappa=0$.  A graph $G$ satisfies \hyperref[def:SC]{\textup{(SC)}}{} if and only if for one (equivalently, all) strictly increasing $\psi\in\mathcal I$, the only $0\le h\in\ell^\infty(X)$ satisfying
\begin{equation}
    -\Delta h=\Psi h
\end{equation}
pointwise on $X$ is $h=0$.  In particular, if $G$ does not satisfy \hyperref[def:SC]{\textup{(SC)}}{}, then for every strictly increasing $\psi\in\mathcal I$ there exists a nontrivial $0\le h\in\ell^\infty(X)$ satisfying~(equation eq:nonlinear-liouville-eq of the paper). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition p:diffeo_conjugation of arXiv:2606.11503, 'Percolation on hierarchical lattices'] Let $U, \tilde{U} \subset \mathbb{R}$ be open sets and consider a $C^{k+1}$ diffeomorphism $f:U \to \tilde{U}$, for some $k \geq 1$. Assume there exists $u_{\star} \in U$ such that $f(u_{\star}) = u_{\star}$ and such that $\zeta = f'(u_{\star})$ satisfies $|\zeta| \neq 1$. There exists a $C^{k}$ diffeomorphism $h: V \to \tilde{V}$ between open neighborhoods of $u_{\star}$ and the origin such that $h(u_{\star}) = 0$ and such that
\begin{equation}
f(x) = h^{-1} \Big( \zeta h(x) \Big), \quad \text{for all } x \in V.
\end{equation}
Furtheremore, the diffeomorphism $h$ is unique up to multiplication by constants. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition of arXiv:2512.09308, 'On asymptotic behavior of solutions to random fractional Riesz-Bessel equations with cycli'] [seneta2006regularly]
A function $L(\cdot)$ is slowly varying at infinity if it is real-valued, positive, and measurable on $[A,\infty)$ for some $A>0$, and satisfies the following condition for every $\lambda >0$:
\begin{equation*}
    \lim_{x\to \infty} \frac{L(\lambda x)}{L(x)}=1.
\end{equation*}

[Lem 9 of arXiv:2609.02398, '\textbf{Convex Order Comparisons for Sub-Gamma Random Variables}'] For all $p \in (0,1)$,
\begin{align*}
    p(1-p)\sqrt{\frac{2\beta_p}{1 - 2p}} \le \frac{1}{2},
\end{align*}
with equality if and only if $p = 1/2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

