{"artifact_digest":"sha256:8c84744389a63323aaa47a597bcafc107d1fa6f95c893c6b8d39318b08098d5e","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/8c/8c84744389a63323aaa47a597bcafc107d1fa6f95c893c6b8d39318b08098d5e.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:1a22ffd94c8485f47b7a99ca1f9fbb40f01dfec7f41e595117fa6e858d418bee","bundle_entry_key":"2412-09290-lemma-16-mom-cum","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s1_127","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s1_127.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2412-09290-lemma-16-mom-cum","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: We will show that for the sequence $(c_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$, where $c_n
  := \Psi^{(n)} (0) / (n - 1) !$, the moment-cumulant relations are
  satisfied, i.e.,
  \begin{equation}
    \ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_n = \sum_{\pi \in \ensuremath{\operatorname{NC}} (n)} \prod_{V \in \pi} c_{|V|},
    \text{\quad for all } \ n \in \mathbb{N}. 
  \end{equation}
  By Leibniz rule we have
  \begin{equation}
    \ensuremath{\boldsymbol{\mu}}_n = \sum_{m = 0}^{n - 1} \frac{n!}{(m + 1) ! (n - m) !}
    \sum_{l_1 + \cdots + l_{n - m} = m} \frac{1}{l_1 ! \ldots l_{n - m} !}
    \Psi^{(l_1 + 1)} (0) \ldots \Psi^{(l_{n - m} + 1)} (0). 
  \end{equation}
