[Theorem thm:entropy-collapse of arXiv:2605.17082, 'Spectral Purification in Reversible Markov Chains: Hidden Parameters, Observable Equivalen'] Under the two-mode approximation, as $k\to\infty$,
\begin{equation}
H(k) = x_k\Bigl(1+\log\tfrac{1}{a_3}+2L_\star k\Bigr) + O\bigl(x_k^2\log(1/x_k)\bigr),
\end{equation}
and consequently
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{H}_k = x_k\Bigl(1+\tfrac{1+\log(1/a_3)}{2L_\star k}\Bigr) + O\Bigl(\tfrac{x_k^2}{k}\log\tfrac1{x_k}\Bigr),
\end{equation}
so that $\mathcal{H}_k/x_k\to1$, and
\begin{equation}
\mathcal{H}_k = G_k\,(1+O(1/k)).
\end{equation}

