[Lem lu of arXiv:2412.09535, 'Local limit theorem for joint subgraph counts'] Let $p$, $\lambda$, $I$, $x_i$ be as in (cor:linear of the paper). For $i \in I$ let $\chi_i = (x_i-p)/\sqrt{p(1-p)}$ and for $S \subseteq I$ let $\chi_S = \prod_{i \in S} \chi_i$. For all $i \in I$, let $\delta_i$ be a real number. Let $\mathcal{S}$ be a collection of subsets of $I$ of size at least $2$ and for all $S \in \mathcal{S}$ let $\delta_S$ be a real number. Suppose $n$ is a positive integer and $\eps > 0$ such that
\begin{cond}
\item \label[scond]{scond:lu1}$\abs{I} \leq n^{1/\eps}$;
\item \label[scond]{scond:lu2}$\abs{S} \leq 1/\eps$ for all $S \in \mathcal{S}$;
\item \label[scond]{scond:lu3}$\abs{\delta_i} \leq 1.2\pi \sqrt{p(1-p)}$ for all $i \in I$;
\item \label[scond]{scond:lu4}$\sum_{i \in I} \delta_i^2 \geq n^\eps$;
\item \label[scond]{scond:lu5}$\sum_{S \in \mathcal{S}} \delta_S^2 \leq n^{-\eps}$.
\end{cond}
Then
\[\abs*{\sete\brac*{e^{i\paren*{\sum_{i \in I} \delta_i \chi_i + \sum_{S \in \mathcal{S}} \delta_S \chi_S}}}} = n^{-\omega_{\lambda,\eps}(1)}.\]

