[Theorem T:graph main of arXiv:2507.01236, 'Disintegration theorem for multifunctions, \\ with applications to empirical Wasserstein d'] Suppose that~$\mu$ has density~$f$ with respect to uniform probability on~$\mathfrak{X}$ such that
\begin{equation}

c \leq f(x) \leq C\mbox{\rm \ for every $x \in \mathfrak{X}$},
\end{equation}
where $0 < c \leq C < \infty$. 
Given $\alpha \in (0, \infty)$, let
\begin{equation}

r(n)\equiv r(n,c, \alpha) := 4 c^{-1} \sqrt{(2 + \alpha) \frac{\ln n}{n}}.
\end{equation}
Then there is $n_0\equiv n_0(c,C,\alpha)$ such that $n\geq n_0$ implies that $(\mathfrak{X},d,\mu)$ is $([|E| (|E| - 1)]^{|E| - 1} n^{ - \alpha},r(n))$-disintegrable (with $0^0$ interpreted as $1$). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 15 (Convexity estimate) of arXiv:2608.25971, 'Positive \texorpdfstring{$\tau$}{tau}-bi-Ricci curvature and Mean curvature flow with surg'] For every $\varepsilon>0$ there exists
$C_\varepsilon=C(n,\alpha,\varepsilon)>0$ such that
\begin{equation}
 \lambda_1\geq-\varepsilon H-C_\varepsilon R^{-1}
\end{equation}
at every point of the smooth flow.

