[Definition 109 (H\"older norms on $\datahypfortimefunctiontwoarg{0}{[\timefunction_0,0) of arXiv:2609.03101, 'The emergence of the Cauchy horizon from the crease for $3D$ compressible Euler flow'] }$]  Let $f$ be a scalar function on $\datahypfortimefunctiontwoarg{0}{[\timefunction_0,0]}$, let $m \geq 0$ be an integer. Then we define the H\"older norm of $f$ relative to geometric coordinates (see the embedding \eqref{E:XMUISMINUSCAPPISAGRAPH}): 
	\begin{align} 
		\begin{split} 
		\| f \|_{C_{\textnormal{data}}^{m,1} \left(\datahypfortimefunctiontwoarg{0}{[\timefunction_0,0]}\right)} & \eqdef \sum_{|\vec{\alpha}| \le m} \max_{(t,x^2,x^3) \in \domainforembeddingdatahypfortimefunctiontwoarg{0}{[0,\mupositive]}} | \mathring{\mathfrak{d}}^{\vec{\alpha}} f(t,h(t,x^2,x^3),x^2,x^3) | \\
		& \ \  + \sum_{|\vec{\alpha}| = m} \sup_{\substack{(t,x^2,x^3),(t_0,x^2_0,x^3_0) \in \domainforembeddingdatahypfortimefunctiontwoarg{0}{[0,\mupositive]} \\ (t,x^2,x^3)\neq(t_0,x^2_0,x^3_0)} } \frac{\left|\mathring{\mathfrak{d}}^{\vec{\alpha}} f(t,h(t,x^2,x^3),x^2,x^3) - \mathring{\mathfrak{d}}^{\vec{\alpha}} f(t_0,h(t_0,x^2_0,x^3_0),x^2_0,x^3_0)\right|}{\textnormal{dist}_{\textnormal{euc}}\left(\big(t,h(t,x^2,x^3),x^2,x^3\big),\big(t_0,h(t_0,x^2_0,x^3_0),x^2_0,x^3_0\big)\right)}.
		\end{split}
	\end{align}

