[Lem lem2.4 of arXiv:2411.14766, 'Axis-Driven Random Walks on $\Z^2$ \\ (transient cases)'] Assume $0<\alpha<1$, for any $z=(x,0)$ or $z=(0,x)$ with $x$ positive and large,
    \begin{align} 
    \mathbb{E}_z(\overline{Z}_{\rho})= x + 2 x^{\alpha}-{\frac{3}{2}}-\frac{1}{6} \frac{1}{x^{\alpha}}+O\Big(\frac{1}{x^{ 2\alpha}}\Big) . 
    \end{align}

For any $\beta \leq 2$, 
\begin{align} 
    \mathbb{E}_z(\overline{Z}_{\rho}^{\beta}) = x^\beta &+2\beta x^{\beta-1+ \alpha}+O( x^{\beta-1}).  

\end{align}

[Lemma lem:gammas of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] The coefficients $\gamma_{q,j,\ell}$ are given by
\begin{align} 
    \gamma_{q,j,\ell}
=
    \frac{(-1)^q2^j}{2^q(2j-1)!!}
    \sum
        \prod_{i=1}^{j-q}
            (\ell+2a_i-i-1/2)
\end{align}
where the sum is taken over all subsets $(a_1, a_2, \dots, a_{j-q})$ of the set $(1,2,\dots, j)$. If $j=q$ then we consider the sum equal to $1$.

