[Lemma lem:firsthalfsum of arXiv:2412.09145, 'Asymptotic expansions for normal deviations of random walks conditioned to stay positive'] Let $a>0,b>1$, $t\in [0,1]$ and $N_n \in [\frac{n}{3}, \frac{2n}{3}-1]$. Then there exists a constant $\gamma_{a,b}$ depending on $a$ and $b$ only, such that
\begin{align*}
    \sum_{k=1}^{N_n} 
    \frac{1}{(n-k-t)^{a}(k+t)^{b}}
    e^{-\frac{z^2}{2 k}}
    \le
    \frac{\gamma_{a,b}}{n^a |z|^{2(b-1)}}.
\end{align*}

