[Proposition prop:asym of arXiv:2607.19844, 'Binomial probabilities at a fixed distance from the mode:\\ size-biasing and the complete '] For every $k\ge1$,
	\begin{equation}
		\widetilde A_k(t;p)-\widetilde A_k(-t;q)=\frac{\Xi_k(p)\,t^{k}}{k},
	\end{equation}
	and
	\begin{equation}
		\sum_{k\ge1}\frac{\Xi_k(p)\,t^{k}}{k\,N^{k}}=\log\frac{q\,m}{p\,(N-m)} ,
	\end{equation}
	which is exactly the ratio of the two size-bias prefactors $Np/m$ and $Nq/(N-m)$.

[Lemma 5 of arXiv:2609.01770, 'Support of Dyson Brownian Motion'] There exists a constant \(c=c(\eps,\sfT,K_0)>0\) such that, for every
\(0\le r\le t\le\sfT\), every \(x\in\mathcal F_t\), and every
\(u\in D_0^{(t,x)}\),
\begin{equation}
  \dist\bigl(\Re z_r(u),S_r\bigr)
  \ge
  \eps-\frac{\eta_*}{2}
  +c\eps(t-r),

\end{equation}
provided \(n\) is sufficiently large.

[Lemma 9 (Endpoint entropy disintegration) of arXiv:2609.02196, 'Schr\"odinger Bridges on Lie Group Manifolds for Probabilistic Intrinsic Generation'] For \(P\ll Q\), \(\Gamma=Y_\#P\), and conditional laws \(P^y,Q^y\),
\begin{equation*}
\KL(P\|Q)=\KL(\Gamma\|\mathcal R_{0T})
+\int\KL(P^y\|Q^y)\,\Gamma(\dd y).
\end{equation*}
Hence, for fixed \(\Gamma\), the unique minimizer is \(P_\Gamma=\int Q^y\Gamma(\dd y)\). (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Prop 14 of arXiv:2510.23423, 'One-arm exponents of the high-dimensional Ising model'] Let $d\geq 2$ and $G=(V,E)$, $H=(V',E')$ be two subgraphs of $\mathbb Z^d$ such that $G\subset H$. Then, for every $A\subset V$, every $J\in (\mathbb R^+)^E$, $J'\in (\mathbb R^+)^{E'}$ satisfying $J_e\leq J_e'$ for $e\in E$, and every $\mathsf{h},\mathsf{h}'\in (\mathbb R^+)^{V(H)}$ satisfying $\mathsf{h}_x\leq \mathsf{h}'_x$ for $x\in V$, one has
\begin{equation}
	\langle \sigma_A\rangle_{G,J,\mathsf{h}}\leq \langle \sigma_A\rangle_{H,J',\mathsf{h}'}.
\end{equation}
Moreover, if we further assume that the restriction of $J'$ to $E$ is equal to $J$, then for every $v\in V$, one has
\begin{equation}
	\langle\sigma_v\rangle^+_{H,J'}\leq \langle \sigma_v\rangle_{G,J}^+.
\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 14 of arXiv:2603.28226, '2603.28226'] Assume that $(\mathcal F_n)_{n\ge1}$ is an $\alpha$-regular atomic filtration. Let $f\in L^1(\Omega,\mathbb P)$ with $f\ge0$, and set $f_n=\mathbb E_n[f]$. Then for every $n\ge2$,
\begin{equation}

 f_n\le \alpha^{-1}f_{n-1}
 \qquad\text{a.s.}
\end{equation}

