[Defi admissible measure of arXiv:2604.21663, 'Large deviations for non-irreducible Markov chains on Euclidean spaces'] A measure $\mu \in \mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$ is said to be \emph{admissible} if 
	\begin{enumerate}
		\item $\mu$ is absolutely continuous with respect to $\mathrm {Leb} $;
		\item $\supp\mu\subseteq \overline C$;
		\item for all $j\in \mathcal J$ such that $\mu(C_j)>0$, we have $\beta\leadsto j$;
		\item the relation $\leadsto$ is a total order on $\{j\in \mathcal J\ |\ \mu(C_j)>0\}$;
	\end{enumerate}
	The set of admissible measures is denoted by $\mathcal A\subseteq \mathcal P(\mathbb R^d)$.

[Prop GR-1 of arXiv:2602.21277, 'A Limit in Law for the Cover Time and Last Visited Vertex of Wired Planar Domains'] There exists a constant $c>0$ such that, if $k$ is large enough, for any $i,j \in \mathbb N$ with $i<j$, $n \geq k$ and $x,\widetilde{x} \in {\rm D}_n$ such that $x \in {\rm B}^-[\widetilde{x};j-1]$ and $\overline{{\rm B}^+[\widetilde{x};j]}\subseteq {\rm D}_n$, we have that 
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\Big( \sqrt{\widehat{N}_t[x;i]} \leq u \,\Big|\, \sqrt{\widehat{N}_t[\widetilde{x};j]} \geq v\,;\mathcal F[\widetilde{x};j]\Big) \leq 2 \exp\bigg\{ -\frac{(v-u)^2}{(j-i+1)k^\gamma}\bigg\}
\end{equation} uniformly over all $t > 0$ and $u,v \in \mathcal N_k$ satisfying that $u\leq v$,  $0 \leq \widetilde{u}_k \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$ and $1 \leq \widetilde{v}_k \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$, as well as  
\begin{equation}
\mathbb{P}\Big( \sqrt{\widehat{N}_t[x;i]} \geq u \,\Big|\, \sqrt{\widehat{N}_t[\widetilde{x};j]} \leq v\,;\mathcal F[\widetilde{x};j]\Big) \leq 2 \exp\bigg\{ -\frac{(u-v)^2}{(j-i+1)k^\gamma}\bigg\}	
\end{equation} uniformly over all $t > 0$ and $u,v \in \mathcal N_k$ satisfying that $v \leq u$,  $0 \leq \widetilde{u}_k \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$ and $1 \leq \widetilde{v}_k \leq {\rm e}^{ck^\gamma}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

