    Let $G$ be a transitive graph of polynomial growth with $d \geq 2$, and suppose that $J : V \times V \to \mathbf{R}_+$ is a transitive kernel with $J(x,y) = \Omega(d_G(x,y)^{-d \alpha})$ with $\alpha > 1$.  

    Then there exists $c = c(G,J) > 0$ such that

    \begin{multline}

        \mathbf{P}_{\beta}
        \left(
            o 
            \leftrightarrow 
            B(r)^c, 
            \# K
            \leq 
            k(r)
        \right) 
        \\
        \leq 
        \sum_{\substack{
            b \in \mathbf{N}
            \\
            \mathbf{m} \in \mathcal{M}(b)
        }}  
        \prod_{i = 0}^{b-1}
        \exp
        \left(
            -c \beta m_i 
