[Definition IM definition of arXiv:2605.16963, 'Stochastic Euler Equations with Pseudo-differential Noise: Continuous and Discontinuous Pe'] A Markov semigroup $\{\mathscr{P}_{t}\}_{t\ge0}$ is called \textbf{Feller} on $E$ if $\mathscr{P}_{t} (C_B(E)) \subset C_B(E)$ for all $t\ge0$. A probability measure $\mu\in\mathbf{P}(E)$ is called an \textbf{invariant probability measure} for $\{\mathscr{P}_{t}\}_{t\ge0}$ if  
		\begin{equation}
			\mathscr{P}^*_{t}\mu=\mu, \quad \text{for all } t > 0.
		\end{equation}

