body:
[Lemma lm:o2 of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] The following holds for almost-every $\omega$. Let $\varphi\in\Phi_\omega$ and let $\xi\in\operatorname{supp}(\varphi)$.  Then for every $\varepsilon>0$ there exists   $T_0 = T_0(\varepsilon,\xi)<0$ such that for all $T<T_0$, there exists an interval $J_{T,\xi}\subseteq \mathbb{R}$ \rm{(}depending on $\varepsilon$\rm{)} such that 
    \begin{equation} 
        (W\star\varphi\,)(x,T)=(\Wf{{\varphi_{I_\varepsilon}}})(x,T)>(\Wf{{\varphi_{I^c_\varepsilon}}})(x,T), \qquad \forall x\in J_{T,\xi}.
    \end{equation}
    Moreover, for every $(x_0,t_0)\in\mathbb{R}^2$, there exists $T_0' = T_0'(\varepsilon,\xi,x_0,t_0) < t_0$ so that for all $T < T_0'$, 
\begin{equation}
        [g^{\xi,L}_{(x_0,t_0)}(T),g^{\xi,R}_{(x_0,t_0)}(T)]\subseteq J_{T,\xi}.
    \end{equation}

