[Proposition prop:right-side-asymptotics of arXiv:2606.19507, 'The $t$-Split Two-Periodic Aztec Diamond Model'] The macroscopic boundary of the $t$-split two-periodic Aztec diamond to the right of the interface is governed by the saddle functions
    \begin{equation}
        \psi_{\beta,i}(z;x,y) = (1+y)\log z - \log(z-1) + \left(\frac{1}{2}-x\right) \log r_{\beta,i}(z), 
    \end{equation}
    for $i = 1,2$. In other words, the macroscopic boundary to the right of the interface is identical to that of the two-periodic model with parameter $\beta$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Corollary 42 of arXiv:2609.04033, 'From configuration spaces to graph complexes via $\mathbf{FA}$-modules'] $$H_\ast(\Pi(n)_{\mathbb{Z}_2}) \cong \begin{cases}
	\Sigma^n sgn_n& \text{ if } n \text{ is odd}, \\
	                0 & \text{ if } n \text{ is even}.
	\end{cases}
$$

