body:
[Lemma lem:vvmeasx_weak_conv of arXiv:2606.11951, 'On Skorokhod Problems for Reflected and Singular Stochastic Heat Equations'] The sequence of vector measures $(\sigma^{(a,\varepsilon_{n,a})})_{n\in\mathbb{N}} \subseteq \mathrm{ca}(\mathcal{B}(L),H_0^{-1})$ converges weakly to $\sigma^{(a)}$, i.e.
	\begin{equation*}
		\sigma^{(a)} \xleftarrow{\;w\;} \sigma^{(a,\varepsilon_{n,a})} \subseteq (\sigma^{(a,1/n)})_{n\in\mathbb{N}}.
	\end{equation*}
	Moreover, for every $h\inH_0^1$, it holds
	\begin{equation}
		\var{\sigma^{(a)}(h,\cdot)}(\cdot) = |\bar{h}_x|\,\mu^{(a)} (\cdot) \quad \text{and} \quad \var{\sigma^{(a)}}(\cdot) = \|\delta_x\|_{H_0^{-1}} \,\mu^{(a)}(\cdot),
	\end{equation}
	which implies that $\sigma^{(a)}$ is bounded w.r.t.\ $\| \cdot \|$ by $(2\pi a(1-a))^{-1/2}$.

