[Theorem thm:mr of arXiv:2605.26048, 'Classification of the eternal solutions and multiple coalescing shocks in the KPZ fixed po'] For almost-every $\omega$, the mapping $\mathcal{H}_\omega[\varphi] := W\star \varphi$ is a homeomorphism $(\Phi_\omega,\mathcal T_{\Phi_\omega}) \to (\mathcal{B}_\omega,\mathcal T_{\mathcal{B}_\omega})$ that satisfies
    \begin{equation} 
    \mathcal{H}[\varphi_1] \vee \mathcal{H}[\varphi_2] = \mathcal{H}[\varphi_1 \vee \varphi_2],\quad \forall \varphi_1,\varphi_2 \in \Phi,
    \end{equation}
    and whose inverse is given by
    \begin{equation} 
    \mathcal{H}^{-1}[b](\xi) = \inf_{(x,t)\in\mathbb{R}^2}\{b(x,t)-W^\xi(0,0;x,t)\},\quad \forall\; b \in \mathcal{B}.
    \end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition def:s-hol of arXiv:2509.08928, 'The near critical random bond Ising model via embedding deformation'] A function $F$ defined on a subset of $\diamondsuit(G)$ is called $s$-holomorphic if, for each pair of adjacent quads $z, z’ \in \diamondsuit(G)$ separated by the edge $[\mathcal{S}(v^\circ(c)); \mathcal{S}(v^\bullet(c))]$ of $\mathcal{S}$ attached to the corner $c$, we have
\begin{equation}

\textrm{Pr}[F(z), \eta_c \mathbb{R}] = \textrm{Pr}[F(z’), \eta_c \mathbb{R}].
\end{equation}

