[Theorem thm:task-symmetry of arXiv:2608.20295, 'Physical-Support Confidence Sets for Highly Coherent Dictionaries'] For every fixed $2\le r\le q-1$ and every interior coefficient vector $x$,
the efficient information contributed by $T$ deployment measurements for an
orientation tangent $\Omega$ is
\begin{equation}
    I_{\Omega\mid x}^{\mathrm{test}}
    =
    \frac{Ts^2}{\sigma^2}
    \chi_{\mathrm{tan}}^2(D,S,x;\Omega).

\end{equation}

Moreover, consider a compact orientation orbit and compact interior
coefficient set $\mathcal X_{\mathrm{orb}}$ for which physical target
separation is of order $s|\phi-\phi'|$ and the coefficient-profiled deployment
mean separation is of order $s\chi_s|\phi-\phi'|$.  Under the precise
regularity conditions stated in Supplementary
Section~(sec:supp-task-orbit of the paper), the minimax physical diameter on this
restricted orbit satisfies
\begin{equation}
\mathcal R_{N,T}^{\mathrm{task}}
(s,\mathcal X_{\mathrm{orb}},\sigma)
\asymp
s
\wedge
\frac{s}{
\sqrt{
    Ns^6
    +
    T\chi_s^2s^2/\sigma^2
}}.

\end{equation} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition prop:explicit_sol of arXiv:2606.29622, 'Affine Structure of the Brownian Signature'] Fix $\bm{\sigma} \in T(\mathbb{C}^2)$. A solution of (equation eq:heat_eq_coef_sig of the paper) with the terminal condition $\bm{u}_T = \bm{\sigma}$ is given by
    \begin{equation}
        \bm{u}_t = \bm{\sigma}|_{\widehat{\mathcal{E}}_{T-t}} = e^{(T-t)\mathscr{L}}\bm{\sigma}, \quad t \in [0, T],
    \end{equation}
    where $e^{(T-t)\mathscr{L}}$ denotes the operator exponential and $\widehat{\mathcal{E}}_{T-t} = \mathbb{E}[\sigW[t, T]] = e^{\otimes(T-t)({\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{0}}} + \frac{1}{2}{\color{NavyBlue}{\mathbf{11}}})}$ denotes the expected time-augmented Brownian signature.

