[Theorem thm:general of arXiv:2607.04620, 'The Exact Ville Identity\\ \large From the Absorbing Case to the General Law\\ with an App'] Let $(M_n)$ be a nonnegative supermartingale with $M_0=1$, let $b>1$, and assume only the integrability condition $\mathbb{E}[M_{T_b}\mathbf{1}(T_b<\infty)]<\infty$. Then the limit in (def:residual of the paper) exists, $0\le R_b<\infty$, and
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{E}[M_{T_b}\mathbf{1}(T_b<\infty)]=1-D_b-R_b,

\end{equation}
so that
\begin{equation}
  \mathbb{P}(T_b<\infty)=\frac{1-D_b-R_b}{b+O_b}.

\end{equation}

