[Lemma 14 ($C^0$-estimate on $u_i$) of arXiv:2608.26619, 'Uniqueness of Positively Curved Ancient Ricci Flows on Surfaces with Boundary'] Let $g_i(t) = u_i(t)g_{0}$ denote the old solutions defined above. Then for each time $t_0<0$, we have the following $C^0$-estimate uniform in $i$:
        \begin{equation}
            \inf_{\psi,i}u_i(\psi,t_0) = \inf_{i}u_i(0,t_0) \geq C(t_0)>0.
        \end{equation}

