body:
[Lem mostlytrans of arXiv:2608.30031, 'Ziggurats, taut foliations, and contact structures'] Let $\mathcal{G}$, $\mathcal{G}'$ be two mostly-transverse $C^0$-foliations on $\mathbb{T}^2$. Then, for every $\varepsilon>0$, there exist $C^0$-foliations $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}'$ such that
    \begin{itemize}
        \item $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}$ and $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}'$ are isotopic, via an $\varepsilon$-$C^{0}$-small isotopy, to $\mathcal{G}$ and $\mathcal{G}'$, respectively,
        \item $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}$ is positively transverse to $\widetilde{\mathcal{G}}'$ everywhere.
    \end{itemize}

[Theorem 39 (Scaling law for Nesterov) of arXiv:2609.02728, 'Momentum in large-batch training: Polyak enlarges the critical batch size, Nesterov improv'] \normalfont
Assume \(\eta<1\) and \(k\gtrsim\max(\eta^{-1}_\rho,(1-\rho)^{-1})\). Then
\begin{equation}

\mathbb E[\cE(\btheta_k)]\eqsim
\begin{cases}
(\eta_\rho k)^{-s}+\dfrac{\sigma^2}{B}\eta_\rho, & 1-\rho\gtrsim\sqrt{\eta},\\[2mm]
N(k)+(\eta_\rho k)^{-s}+\dfrac{\sigma^2}{B}\min\{\eta_\rho,\eta_\rho^{1/\beta}\}, & \dfrac{\eta}{B^\beta}\lesssim1-\rho\lesssim\sqrt{\eta},
\end{cases}
\end{equation}
where \(N(k)\) denotes the underdamped transient and satisfies \(0\leq N(k)\lesssim\min\{1,(\eta k)^{-s}\}\rho^k\). If \(1-\rho\lesssim\eta/B^\beta\), the dynamics are not risk stable. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

