[Theorem thm of arXiv:2411.01731, '$L^2$-Wasserstein contraction of modified Euler schemes for SDEs with high diffusivity and'] Assume that   $({\bf A}_1)$ and $({\bf H}_1)$-$({\bf H}_3)$ hold.
Then,
   for all  $\delta\in(0,\delta_1^\star]$,  $n\ge0$, and $\mu,\nu\in\mathscr P_2(\mathds R^d)$,
\begin{align}
\mathbb W_2\big(\mu P^{(\delta)}_{n\delta},\nu P^{(\delta)}_{n\delta}\big)\le C_0\text{\rm{e}}^{-\frac{1}{2}(\lambda_1\wedge\lambda_2) n\delta}\mathbb W_2(\mu,\nu),
\end{align}
where $\lambda_1,\lambda_2, C_0$ and $\delta^\star_1$ were defined in (equation WQ* of the paper) and (equation dd1 of the paper), respectively. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

