[Lemma 16 (Deterministic inversion through order one) of arXiv:2608.20101, '\bfseries Largest bulk gap of the complex Ginibre ensemble'] Let \(L\to\infty\), put \(u=2\sqrt L\), \(\ell=\log u\), and define
\begin{equation}
 \beta=\beta(L):=u^2-2u\ell+4a_2u+4a_1u^{1/2}
 +2\ell^2+\left(\frac{10}{3}-8a_2\right)\ell
 +8a_2^2-4a_2+4a_0.
\end{equation}
Uniformly for \(x\) in a fixed compact subset of \(\R\),
\begin{equation}
 \Phi\bigl((\beta+4x)^{1/4}\bigr)
 =L+x+O\!\left(\frac{\ell^3}{\sqrt u}\right).
\end{equation}

[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2607.11756, 'Full replica symmetry breaking in the Sherrington--Kirkpatrick model'] The processes above satisfy
\begin{align}
 \dd M_s&=\beta C_s\dd W_s,\\
 \dd C_s&=-\beta^2\alpha(s)C_s^2\dd s+\beta D_s\dd W_s,
 \\
 \dd D_s&=-3\beta^2\alpha(s)C_sD_s\dd s+\beta A_s\dd W_s.

\end{align}
Consequently,
\begin{equation}
 \Gamma'(s)=\beta^2\E C_s^2,
\end{equation}
and
\begin{equation}
 \Gamma'(t)-\Gamma'(r)=\beta^4\int_r^t
 \E[D_s^2-2\alpha(s)C_s^3]\dd s.
\end{equation}
If $\alpha(s)=m$ on an open interval $I$, then $\Gamma\in C^3(I)$ and
\begin{align}
 \Gamma''(s)&=\beta^4\E[D_s^2-2mC_s^3],
 \\
 \Gamma'''(s)&=\beta^6\E[A_s^2-12mC_sD_s^2+6m^2C_s^4].

\end{align}

