body:
[Lemma 6 of arXiv:2607.17087, 'Transportation-cost inequalities for invariant measures of stochastic reaction-diffusion e'] Let $p_{t}(x,y)$ be the heat kernel of the operator $\frac{1}{2}\partial_{xx}$ on $[0,1]$ with the Dirichlet boundary condition, and
\begin{align*}
 P_t f(x) := \int_{0}^{1} p_{t}(x,y) f(y)dy, \quad x\in [0,1].
\end{align*}
Then for any $p> 1$,
\begin{align}
  \sup_{x\in [0,1]} |P_t f(x)| \leq C_{p\rightarrow\infty} t^{-\frac{1}{2p}}\Vert f\Vert_{L^p([0,1])},
\end{align}
where
\begin{align}
  C_{p\rightarrow\infty}:= (2\pi)^{-\frac1{2p}} \left(\frac{p-1}{p}\right)^{\frac{p-1}{2p}}.
\end{align}
The constant $C_{p\rightarrow\infty}$ can be bounded by
\begin{align}
  C_{p\rightarrow\infty} \leq \left(\frac{1}{2\sqrt{\pi}}\right)^{\frac{1}{p}}.
\end{align}

