[Lemma lem:local-arithmetic of arXiv:2609.00777, 'Universal murmuration and Hecke augmentation'] Let $D,M\geq1$ and $1\leq r<2\sqrt Q/\sqrt{X+Y}$ with $P\nmid r$.
The series
\[
\sum_{\substack{d,n\geq1\\ (r,d)\ {\rm admissible}}}
\frac{\Gamma_{r,Q}(d,n)}{nd}
\]
is absolutely convergent, and
\begin{equation}
\sum_{\substack{d\leq D,\ n\leq M\\ (r,d)\ {\rm admissible}}}
\frac{\Gamma_{r,Q}(d,n)}{nd}
=BC(r)+O(P^{-2})
+O_\varepsilon\left(
(QDM)^\varepsilon\left(D^{-2}+M^{-1/5}\right)
\right).
\end{equation}
The constants and tail bounds are uniform in the displayed range of $r$; $k$ remains fixed.

[Lemma lem:interior_intersection_left_first of arXiv:2507.15589, 'Tightness of approximations to metrics on non-simple conformal loop ensemble gaskets'] Fix $a_1 >0$, $p \in (0,1)$. Suppose that we have the setup of Section~(se:bubble_setup of the paper) with $(D,x_0,y_0) = (\delta\mathbf{D},-i\delta,i\delta)$. Let $z_1,w_1 \in \partial B(0,\delta/2)$. Let $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ be the angle $\theta_0$ flow line starting from $z_1$, stopped upon exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$. Let $\eta_{w_1}^L$ be the angle $+\pi/2$ flow line starting from $w_1$, stopped upon hitting $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ or exiting $B(0,3\delta/4)$ (whichever occurs first). In case $\eta_{w_1}^L$ intersects $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ in $B(0,\delta/4)$, let $\overline{w}$ denote the intersection point, and let $\overline{\eta}^R$ be the angle $-\pi/2$ flow line starting from $\overline{w}$, reflecting off $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ in the opposite direction, and stopped upon exiting $B(0,\delta/4)$. Sample the internal metric in the regions bounded between $\overline{\eta}^R$ and $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$. 
Let $E^p$ be the event that the following hold.
\begin{itemize}
\item $\eta_{w_1}^L$ intersects the right side of $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ with an angle difference of $\pi/2 - \theta_0$, and they do not intersect in any other way.
\item There exist $x',x,y,y' \in \eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0} \cap \overline{\eta}^R$ such that $(x,y) \in \intptsapproxbubble{U_{x',y'}}{\epsilon}$ as in~(equation eq:intpts_bubble of the paper) and $U_{x',y'} \subseteq B(0,\delta^{1+a_1})$ and $\metapproxacres{\epsilon}{U_{x',y'}}{x}{y}{\Gamma} \geq \median{\epsilon}+\epsilon^{-a_0}\mathbf{a}_{\epsilon}$.
\item The following event has conditional probability at least $p$ given $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$, $\eta_{w_1}^L$, $\overline{\eta}^R$, $X_\delta^{\theta_0}$, $X_\delta^{+\pi/2}$, and the values of $h$ on these sets:
\begin{itemize}
\item The flow line $\eta_0$ merges into $\eta_{z_1}^{\theta_0}$ before entering $B(0,\delta/4)$.
\item There exists a flow line with angle $+\pi/2$ starting from a point on $\eta_2$ that merges into $\eta_{w_1}^L$ before intersecting $\eta_0$.
\end{itemize}
\end{itemize}
Then $\mathbf{P}[E^p] = O(\delta^{{\alpha_{\mathrm{apr}}}})$ as $\delta \to 0$.

