[Lem excursionpartition of arXiv:2411.12149, 'Airy limit for $\beta$-additions through Dunkl operators'] For $H\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 0}$, $L\in \mathbb{Z}_{\ge 1}$, the partition function for the walk bridges with length $L$ from $H$ to $0$ is 
\begin{equation}
  |\mathcal{W}(H,0,L;N)|=\frac{H+1}{L+1}|\tilde{W}(H+1,L+1;N)|z_{c}(N)=\frac{H+1}{L+1} \frac{1}{2\pi i} \oint\; \left(\frac{z}{z_c(N)}\right)^H V_{N}(z)^{L+1} \; dz
\end{equation}
where our contour only encloses the pole at zero. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lem TeLe1 of arXiv:2411.06974, '{\bf Distribution dependent SDEs with multiplicative fractional noise}'] Let $x,y$ be two positive constants and $0<\alpha<\beta<1$. Then for any $0<r<s$, we have
\begin{align*}
\int_s^r\frac { (x(r-u)^\beta)\wedge y } {(r-u)^{\alpha+1}}\text{\rm{d}} u\leq \frac {4\beta} {(\beta-\alpha)\alpha}x^{\frac {\alpha} {\beta}}y^{\frac {\beta-\alpha} {\beta}}.
\end{align*}

