body:
[Lemma lem:information-propagation of arXiv:2605.08052, 'Rapid phase ordering of Ising dynamics on $\mathbb Z^2$'] There exists $M_0(d),\ell_0(d)$ such that as long as $M$ in~(equation eq:spatial-scale of the paper) is larger than $M_0$, then for every $k$ and every $B\in \mathscr{B}_k$, the probability 
    \begin{align*}
        \mathbb P(\mathsf{InfProp}_k(B)^c )\le  e^{ - \ell_k/10}\,.
    \end{align*}

