[Thm 3 of arXiv:2606.07194, 'Survival Probability of Markov Linear Reccurence Sequence in a Random Environment: Subcrit'] {(Theorem 2.2 and Corollary 2.5 of~\cite{QSDNew}).}

Under the conditions of~Theorem~\ref{MainQSTh} 
$$
\pi_i = \frac{R-1}{{\bf E} \left(\left.R^{T_{i}}T_i; T_i<T_0\right|X_0=i\right)}, i\in \mathbb{N},
$$
where $T_i$ is the first return to the state $i$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 19 of arXiv:2609.01460, 'On cost-induced Santal\'o-type inequalities \\ in Polish measure spaces'] Let $m\in \N$ and let, for $i=1,\dots,m$, $(X_i,d_i,\mu_i)$ be Polish measure spaces and consider collections of analytic sets $\mathcal{A}_i\subset 2^{X_i}$. Let $-\infty \leq a<b \leq +\infty$ and let $\Phi:X_1\times\cdots \times X_m\to (a,b)$ be a continuous function.

    Then, the operator $\square f: (a,b) \to [0,\infty]$ given by
\begin{equation*}
\square f(r) = \sup_{\{x= (x_1,\dots,x_m) \colon \Phi(x) \geq r\} }\mathcal{M}_p^{(t)}(f), \quad -\infty < p \leq 1,
\end{equation*}
where $f\in \mathcal{F}\left(\mathcal{A}_1\right)\times \cdots\times \mathcal{F}\left(\mathcal{A}_m\right)$, is a generalized supremal convolution.

[Lemma lem:upper-heat of arXiv:2608.20537, 'Persistent anisotropy in multi-dimensional\\ branching Brownian motion'] Suppose $\beta$ satisfies (equation eq:beta-dot of the paper) and (equation eq:necessary of the paper).
  Then there exist constants $t_{\textnormal{max}} \leq -1$ and $C > 0$ such that the minimal positive ancient solution of (equation eq:upper-heat of the paper) satisfies
  \begin{equation}

    v(t, y) \leq C(y + 1) \quad \text{for all } t \leq t_{\textnormal{max}},\enspace y > 0.
  \end{equation}

