[Lemma 13 (Moser iteration step) of arXiv:2608.26834, 'Small-time annealed large deviations principle for one-dimensional diffusions in a random '] Assume that $Q_1\subset(0,S)\times {[-R,R]}$ and let $u\ge0$ be a bounded weak sub-solution to equation (\ref{02}) on $Q_1$. There is an absolute constant $C$ such that, for every $p\ge2$ and $1/2\le\lambda'<\lambda\le1$,
		\begin{equation}
			\|u\|_{L^{3p}(Q_{\lambda'},\mu_W\dd s)}
			\le\left(\frac{Ce^{cM_R}p^2}{(\lambda-\lambda')^2\ell^2}\right)^{1/p}
			\|u\|_{L^p(Q_\lambda,\mu_W\dd s)}.
