{"artifact_digest":"sha256:f2b79db673969c565023607199ba5ed50c2890e8bff4a4d721750482a8d2da83","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/f2/f2b79db673969c565023607199ba5ed50c2890e8bff4a4d721750482a8d2da83.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:8a0fb3d41d84eb259f1b62a37548388734d3d56dfc53fea5e1f88745010c1669","bundle_entry_key":"2605-21638-lemma-19-restricted","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_035","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_035.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-21638-lem-19-restricted","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Let $h\colon\R_+\to \R$ be a measurable bounded function and $\mathscr C_N = \sigma(Z_j, j \in \Z\setminus \{1,\ldots,N\})$. 
Further let $Y$ be a $\mathscr C_N$-measurable bounded function. 
Then 
\begin{align*}
	\E\bigl[ \1_{\{(Z_1,\ldots, Z_N)\in A\}} h(Z_1+\cdots+ Z_N) Y\bigr] 
	& =  \E\Bigl[ Y \E\bigl[ \1_{\{(Z_1,\ldots, Z_N)\in A\}} h(Z_1+\cdots+ Z_N) \mid \mathscr C_N \bigr]\Bigr]
\end{align*} 
By Lemma~\ref{lem:spacinggibbs} and an elementary change of variables, the conditional expectation on the right side is equal to
\begin{multline*}
	\frac{1}{\mathrm{norm.}}\int_{N r_\mathrm{hc}}^\infty \e^{-p L} h(L) \Biggl\{ \int_{(r_\mathrm{hc},\infty)^N} \1_A(\vect z') \exp\bigl( - \mathscr ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:bc2fb5fa55a64041b953a519b056d6351fb229158872180ef8507df4c0d896b7","revision_digest":"sha256:95c8c05f2ef42fbe2a1f1b05ead37d8d745f1747cba0e77807174f585b1698d4","source_id":"arxiv:2605.21638","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

