{"artifact_digest":"sha256:dccd367b8329d293ae8536705da017344a82e5852a69c14f8fbebbd4966cb865","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/dc/dccd367b8329d293ae8536705da017344a82e5852a69c14f8fbebbd4966cb865.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:2a3526a069e58eb54d8f0027118c05c057248309b1d4530b297c337872e45f59","bundle_entry_key":"2510-13659-lemma-34-upper-gradient","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_060","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-v2-20260907/bundle_s0_060.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2510-13659-lemma-34-upper-gradient","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Let $\gamma:[0,L] \to \mathbb{R}^n$ be any rectifiable curve  with arc length parametrization. 
		Note that 
		\begin{equation} 
