[Theorem th:Schauder_est_intr of arXiv:2608.30493, '\bf McKean-Vlasov Differential Equations:\\ {An introduction and a focus on some kinetic m'] For any $\alpha,\gamma\geq 0 $ and $T>0$, there exists $C=C(\alpha,\gamma,T,B)>0$ such that 
\begin{align}
 \|\mathscr{P}'_{\cdot}\, \varphi\|_{\mathcal{C}_B^{\alpha+\gamma}((r,T)\times\mathbb{R}^d)}  &\leq C\, r^{-\frac{\alpha}{2}} \|\varphi\|_{B,\gamma},\\ 
\|\mathscr{P}_{T-\cdot}\, \varphi\|_{{\mathcal{C}_B^{\alpha+\gamma}((0,T-r)\times\mathbb{R}^d)} }& \leq C\, (T-r)^{-\frac{\alpha}{2}} \|\varphi\|_{B,\gamma}, 
\end{align}
for any  $r\in (0,T)$ and for any $\varphi\in C^{b}(\mathbb{R}^d)$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

