[Def1 definition:snaketrajectory of arXiv:2411.12717, 'Excursion theory for Markov processes indexed by Lévy trees'] Fix ${\mathrm{w}} \in \mathcal{W}_E$. A continuous function  $\omega:\mathbb{R}_+ \to \mathcal{W}_E$   started at  $\omega_0 = {\mathrm{w}}$
 and  satisfying for any $s,t \geq 0$,  that 
  \begin{equation}
    \omega_{s}(r) = \omega_{t}(r),  \quad \quad  \text{ for every } \, \,  0 \leq r \leq m_{\zeta(\omega)}(s ,t),
\end{equation}
will be referred to as a snake trajectory started from ${\mathrm{w}}$.  We denote  the collection of snake trajectories started from  ${\mathrm{w}}$ by $\mathcal{S}^\circ_{{\mathrm{w}}}$, and we write  
\begin{equation*}
    \mathcal{S}^\circ := \bigcup_{{\mathrm{w}} \in \mathcal{W}_E} \mathcal{S}^\circ_{\mathrm{w}} ,
\end{equation*}
for the set of all snake trajectories.\footnote{Note that [ALG15] defines a snake trajectory under the additional conditions that $\omega$ starts from  some $y \in E$  (instead of a general path ${\mathrm{w}} \in \mathcal{W}_E$)  and that $\sigma(\omega)$ is  finite.}

