Let $\mathcal{T}$ be a big tensor-triangulated category with compact objects $\mathcal{T}^c$. The homological support of an object $X \in \mathcal{T}$ is the subset $\operatorname{supp}_*(X) \subset \operatorname{Spc}(\mathcal{T}^c)$ consisting of all prime ideals $\mathfrak{p}$ such that $\Gamma_\mathfrak{p} X \neq 0$, where $\Gamma_\mathfrak{p}$ is the local cohomology functor at $\mathfrak{p}$.
\mathcal{T} is compactly generated tt-category
\Gamma_\mathfrak{p} is the local cohomology functor at prime \mathfrak{p}

[Lemma lem:basic-props of arXiv:2605.10617, 'Logarithmic scaling of selective sweep curves:\\ from tents to houses'] Let $Z=(Z(t), t \geq 0)$ be a continuous-time binary Galton--Watson process with birth rate $b$ and death rate $d$  being strictly positive such that $b \neq d$, and assume $Z(0)=1$. Then for $t\ge0 $
    \begin{equation}
                \mathbb{P}(Z(t)\geq j)
             = \frac{b-d}{b-de^{-(b-d)t}}\cdot\Big(1-\frac{b-d}{be^{(b-d)t}-d}\Big)^{j-1}.
    \end{equation}

