[Lemma lem:characnf of arXiv:2505.12187, 'Speeding up quantum Markov processes through lifting'] Let $\mathcal{P}_t = \exp(t \mathcal{L})$ be a QMS with an invariant state $\sigma \in \mathcal{D}_+(\mathcal{M})$, and $\mathcal{F}(\mathcal{L})$ and $\mathcal{N}(\mathcal{L})$ be the subalgebras defined in (equation def:fixedpointspace of the paper) and (equation def:decoherence of the paper). Then,
    \begin{itemize}
        \item Any purely imaginary eigenvalue $\lambda = i \mu$ with $\mu \in \mathbb{R}$ of $\mathcal{L}$ is simple, namely, the associated Jordan block is of size one. 
        \item Define $V_0 := {\rm Span}\{X \in \mathcal{M}\,;\ \mathcal{L}(X) = i \mu X \ \text{for some $\mu \in \mathbb{R}$}\}$, and let $V_-$ be the direct sum of generalized eigenspaces of $\mathcal{L}$ associated with eigenvalues $\lambda$ with $\mathfrak{Re}(\lambda) < 0$. 
        We have 
        \begin{equation*}
            V_0 = \mathcal{N}(\mathcal{L})\,, \quad V_- = \{X \in \mathcal{M}\,;\ \lim_{t \to \infty} \mathcal{P}_t(X) = 0\}\,,
        \end{equation*}
        and the orthogonal decomposition with respect to both $\sigma$-GNS and KMS inner products:
        \begin{align*}
            \mathcal{M} =  V_0 \oplus V_-\,.
        \end{align*}
    \end{itemize} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 55 of arXiv:2607.21374, 'Local structure at the maximum and sharp persistence asymptotics of rough fractional Brown'] Fix \(K<\infty\) and \(\kappa\in(0,H)\).  There is
\(C_{K,\kappa}<\infty\) with the following property.  For parameters
\(h,u,L\) satisfying \eqref{eq:block-repulsion-component-range}, under
\(\widehat Q_{h,u,L}\), and for every dyadic \(r=2^j\geq2\) whose
displayed interval is nonempty,
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
  &\widehat Q_{h,u,L}\left(
    \inf_{r\leq s\leq\min(2r,L)}G_s<r^{H-\kappa}
  \right)\\
  &\qquad\leq
  C_{K,\kappa}\left[
    r^{-\kappa}
    +(1+\sqrt{\log r})r^{-(H-\kappa)}
  \right].
\end{split}

\end{equation}

