[Corollary 21 (Threshold form) of arXiv:2605.11451, '2605.11451'] Define
\begin{equation}
 R_{p,n}:=\frac{m_{4,p,n}}{v_{p,n}^2}
 =
 \frac{\Gamma(5/p)\Gamma(1/p)}{\Gamma(3/p)^2}
 \frac{\Gamma(1+(n+2)/p)^2}
 {\Gamma(1+n/p)\Gamma(1+(n+4)/p)}.
\end{equation}
Then $\Phi_{p,n}$ is nonmonotone if $R_{p,n}<3$ and strictly decreasing if $R_{p,n}\ge3$.
For every fixed $1\le p<2$, the sequence $n\mapsto R_{p,n}$ is strictly increasing and has limit
\begin{equation}
 R_{p,\infty}=\frac{\Gamma(5/p)\Gamma(1/p)}{\Gamma(3/p)^2}>3.
\end{equation}
Consequently there is a finite threshold
\[
 N(p):=\min\{n\ge2:R_{p,n}\ge3\}
\]
such that $\Phi_{p,n}$ is nonmonotone for $n<N(p)$ and strictly decreasing for $n\ge N(p)$.

[Thm 2 of arXiv:2604.07370, 'Probabilistic Weyl law for twisted Toeplitz matrices with rough symbols'] Let $p\in \mathscr{C}^{0,\varrho}_{\mathrm{pw}}S_d$ and $\mathscr{U}_p$ be given by \eqref{Ensemble des singularités}. Assume that $p$ satisfies Assumptions \ref{Hypothèse théorème final - volume singularités} and \ref{Hypothèse théorème final - volume préimage}. Let $Q_N$ be an $N^d\times N^d$ random matrix satisfying Assumption \ref{Hypothèse théorème final - matrice aléatoire} for some $\kappa_3>0$. Then, for every $\delta_0>0$, setting 
    \begin{equation}
        \delta:=N^{-(\kappa_3+\delta_0)},

    \end{equation}
     the empirical spectral measure 
     \begin{equation}
        \mu_{N}:=\frac{1}{N^d}\sum_{\lambda\in \sigma(M_N(p)+\delta Q_N)}\delta_{\lambda}

    \end{equation}
     of $M_N(p)+\delta Q_N$ converges weakly in probability to the push-forward $p_*\mathrm{L}$ of the normalized Lebesgue measure on $[0,1]^d_x\times \T_\xi^{d}$ by $p$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition cocycle of arXiv:2507.08757, 'Strong existence and uniqueness of the tilt-indexed Busemann process in the planar corner '] A function $A:\mathbb{Z}^2\times\mathbb{Z}^2\to\mathbb{R}$ is a \emph{cocycle} if 
\begin{equation}\begin{aligned}
A(x,y)+A(y,z)=A(y,z)\quad\text{for all }x,y,z\in\mathbb{Z}^2.
\end{aligned}\qedhere\end{equation}

[Proposition P:I to L_interval of arXiv:2507.01236, 'Disintegration theorem for multifunctions, \\ with applications to empirical Wasserstein d'] Let~$\mu$ be arbitrarily specified.  If 
a set $I \in 2^{[n]}$ is irreducible, then there exists $L \supseteq I$ such that~$L$ is connected in the usual path-graph (call it 
$\mathcal{P}_n$) on $[n]$ and
\begin{equation}

\cup_{i \in I} B_i = \cup_{i \in L} B_i.
\end{equation}

[Lemma 12 (Collision-null diffuse basis) of arXiv:2608.12492, 'Weak Limits of Wiener Chaos: Primitive--Fock Classification and Hilbert--Stein Extraction'] The family in \eqref{primitive:eq:spatial-replicas} satisfies:
\begin{enumerate}[label=\textup{(\roman*)}]
 \item
 \begin{equation}
  s!\ip{u_{N,s,\alpha}}{u_{N,s,\beta}}
  =\1_{\{\alpha=\beta\}};

 \end{equation}
 \item for every $1\le r<s$,
 \begin{equation}
  \norm{u_{N,s,\alpha}\otimes_ru_{N,s,\beta}}
  \le \frac{C_{s,r}}{\sqrt N}
  \1_{\{\alpha=\beta\}};

 \end{equation}
 \item every $u_{N,s,\alpha}$ vanishes whenever two of its spatial
 variables are at distance less than $1$.
\end{enumerate}

[Lemma l:iteration_enhanced of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $R>0$, $M\geq 1$ and $\eta\in (0,1)$. Let $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ be such that (equation eq:condition_pq_subcritical_scaling_cutoff of the paper) holds.
Then, there exist $\mu_0>0$ and $N_0\geq 1$ such that, for all $\mu\geq \mu_0$, $N\geq N_0$ and $n\geq 1$, the $(p,q)$-solution to (equation eq:navier_stokes_cutoff_mixing of the paper) provided by Lemma (l:global_cutoff of the paper) with data $u_0\in \mathcal{B}_{p,q}(M)$ satisfies
\begin{equation}

{\mathbf E}\|w_{{\rm cut}}^N(n+1)\|^2_{L^2}\leq \eta \,{\mathbf E}\|w_{{\rm cut}}^N (n)\|^2_{L^2}.
\end{equation}

