[Thm cor:almost_legendre of arXiv:2506.12171, 'The multinomial dimer model'] Fix $\Lambda$. Let $w_1,\dots,w_D$ be periodic edge weights satisfying (equation eq:gauge_change_loop of the paper) for contractible loops, and suppose that $s=\sum_{i=1}^D p_i e_i$, where $p_i = \frac{w_i}{w_1+\dots+w_D}$. Then the surface tension is minus the entropy of $\mu_{n,N,w}$, i.e.,
    \begin{align*}
        \sigma(s) = \frac{1}{w_1+\dots+w_D}\sum_{i=1}^D w_i \log w_i - F(w). 
    \end{align*}

