[Lemma l:intermediate_estimate_pressure_deterministic0 of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Under the assumptions of Theorem (t:caccioppoli of the paper), for all $\alpha\in (0,1)$,  it holds that  
\begin{align*}
\Big({\mathbf E}\sup_{\alpha I}\Big\|v-\fint_{\alpha B} v\Big\|_{L^2(\alpha B)}^r\Big)^{1/r}
&+
\big({\mathbf E}\|\nabla v\|_{L^2(\alpha Q)}^r\big)^{1/r}\\
&+
\big({\mathbf E}\|(\nabla \widetilde{\pi}_n)_n\|_{L^{2}(\alpha Q;\ell^2)}^r\big)^{1/r}
\leq C_0 \mathcal{E}_{Q}^{\#} ,
\end{align*}
where $C_0$ depends only on $d,M,\varrho,\nu,\nu_0,r$ and $\alpha$ and $\mathcal{E}_Q^{\#}$ is as in (equation eq:def_En_Q_caccioppoli of the paper).

