where $\eta=(\eta_{1}, \cdots,\eta_{n})^{\top}$ and $\tilde{\eta}$ is an independent copy of $\eta$.

 For convienence, denote by $d_{2}$ and $d_{\alpha^{*}}$ the distance on $\mathcal{A}$ induced by $\Vert\cdot\Vert_{l_{2}\to ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:dcfac66bde4b3d3a93651e576c6e8cc626193eaf5084f3eae8d09b05808d7636","revision_digest":"sha256:9f84fb8d980c667bcc9459fecb7139b12fdac77049f0ec03fa553282820c77d0","source_id":"arxiv:2411.08430","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-08","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

