[Lm Tightness Lemma of arXiv:2411.01633, 'On the Limit of the Tridiagonal Model \\for $\beta$-Dyson Brownian Motion'] Fixing a $\delta>0$, for $n$ large enough we have
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{P}\bigg(\sup_{t,s \in [0,T]}\bigg|\frac{G(M(t)/\sqrt{n},\theta(t))-G(M(s)/\sqrt{n},\theta(s))}{|t-s|^{1/2-\delta}}\bigg|>u\bigg) \leq Ce^{-c \frac{u^2}{\log(n)}}+Ce^{-c\frac{n}{\log(n)}},
    \end{equation*}
    where $C,c$ may depend on $T$ and $\delta$.

