[Theorem 10 of arXiv:2608.25094, 'Noising-Denoising by Large Temperature Schr\"{o}dinger Bridges'] Let $(M,g)$ be either (1) $\mathbb{R}^{d}$ with \eqref{eq:OU} reference process, or (2) a compact manifold with reference process \eqref{eq:reference-process-intro} satisfying $U \in C^2(M)$. Let $\mu,\nu \in \cP_2(M)$ satisfy Assumption \ref{assumption}. The following limit holds
    \begin{align*}
        \lim\limits_{T \to +\infty} \exp(\lambda_1 T)\left(H(P^{T}|R^{T}) - \left(H(\mu|\diffref)+H(\nu|\diffref)\right)\right) &= -\sum_{i \in \mathcal{I}_{1}} p_iq_i,
    \end{align*}
    where $p_i = \langle \psi_i, \rho\rangle_{L^2(\diffref)}$ and $q_i = \langle \psi_i,\sigma \rangle_{L^2(\diffref)}$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

