[Theorem 36 of arXiv:2608.27630, 'Oriented planar maps and \\ annular mating of trees'] Let $\gamma\in(0,2)\backslash\{\sqrt2\}$. There is a constant $C_\gamma>0$ such that for every $b>0$, the above boundary length process for 
    \begin{equation}
         \int_0^\infty \MT(\ell,b,\ell+a)\,\d\ell
    \end{equation}
   has law $C_\gamma B_{0,-a+bi}^{\gamma;\bbH}$. Furthermore, it is possible to define the map $F$ introduced below Definition~\ref{def:Quantum-cell} such that it a.s.\ recovers the decorated LQG surface from its boundary length process.

[Theorem t:almost_Linfty of arXiv:2607.15140, 'On the absence of blow-up in the 3D Navier-Stokes equations with transport noise'] Fix $0<T<\infty$. Let $p,q\in (2,\infty)$ be such that 
\begin{equation}

\frac{2}{p}+\frac{d}{q}<1.
\end{equation}
Then for all $r\in (1,\infty)$ there exists $C_0>0$ such that for any $N$, any interval $I=(t_0-T,t_0)\subset (-1/4,\infty)$ with length $T<\infty$, and
\begin{equation}

F,G\in L^r_{\mathscr{P}}(\Omega; L^p(I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d;{\mathbb R}^{d\times d}))),
\end{equation}
satisfying
\begin{equation}

\mathrm{Tr} (G)=0 \text{ a.e.\ on }\mathbb{T}^d \qquad \text{ and }\qquad \nabla \cdot G =0\text{ in }\mathscr{D}'(\mathbb{T}^d),
\end{equation} 
a.e.\ on $I\times \Omega$, it holds that 
\begin{align}

\sup_{ I\times \mathbb{T}^d}\big( {\mathbf E}|v^N|^r \big)^{1/r}
&\leq C_0  \big({\mathbf E}\|F\|_{L^p( I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^r\big)^{1/r}+ C_0 \big({\mathbf E}\|G\|_{L^p( I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^r\big)^{1/r},
\end{align}
where $v^N$ is the unique energy solution to (equation eq:turbulent_Stokes_scaling_uniform_estimates_modified of the paper).
In particular, for all $r_0\in (1,\infty)$, there exists $C_1>0$ independent of $N,t_0,F$ and $G$ for which  
\begin{align}

\big( {\mathbf E}\|v^N\|_{L^{r_0}( I\times \mathbb{T}^d)}^{r} \big)^{1/{r}}
\leq C_1  \big({\mathbf E}\|F\|_{L^p( I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^{r}\big)^{1/r}+ C_1 \big({\mathbf E}\|G\|_{L^p( I;L^q(\mathbb{T}^d))}^{r}\big)^{1/{r}}.
\end{align} (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Lemma 19 of arXiv:2606.02036, 'Self-intersection local times for Volterra Gaussian processes in stochastic flows with int'] The random process $\{\cT_k(t): t \geqslant 0\}$ is a positive continuous square integrable martingale with respect to $\tilde{\cF}_t$ with quadratic variation
\begin{align*}
&{}\langle\cT_k\rangle(t)=(k-1)^2\int_{\mbR^d}\int_{\mbR^d}\int^t_0\cE_k(v_1,s)\cE_k(v_2,s)

\left(\sum^d_{i=1}\D b_{ii}*\D b_{ii}(x(v_2,s)-x(v_1,s))\right)\differential{s} \nu_k(\differential{v_1})\nu_k(\differential{v_2}).
\end{align*}

