[Lemma 14 (Compact embedding of paths) of arXiv:2606.16636, 'Free energy of non-convex multi-species spin glasses with centered Ising spins'] Let $r\in(1,+\infty]$, and let $(q_n)_{n\in\N}$ be a sequence in $\mcl Q_r^\sS$ such that
\begin{align*}
    \sup_{n\in\N} \Ll|q_n\Rr|_{L^r}<+\infty.
\end{align*}
There exists a subsequence $\Ll(q_{n_k}\Rr)_{k\in\N}$ and some $q\in\mcl Q_r^\sS$ such that, for every $r'\in [1,r)$, this subsequence converges almost everywhere on $[0,1]$ and in $L^{r'}$ to $q$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

