[Definition of arXiv:2411.17653, 'Exclusion processes with non-reversible boundary: hydrodynamics and large deviations'] Given $\gamma\in{\mathcalboondox M}_{ac}$, let $\Pi_\gamma$ be the set of paths $\pi(t,dx)=\rho_t(x)dx$ in $\mathcal{D}([0,T],{\mathcalboondox M}_{ac})$ such that
    \begin{enumerate}
        \item There exists a $t_0>0$ such that $\rho$ follows the hydrodynamic equation (equation PDEproblem of the paper) in the interval $[0,t_0]$.
        \item For every $0<\delta\leq T,\;\exists\;\varepsilon>0$ such that $\varepsilon\leq\rho_t(x)\leq1-\varepsilon$ for all $(t,x)\in  {[\delta,T]}\times[0,1].$
        \item $\rho$ is smooth in $(0,T]\times[0,1].$
    \end{enumerate}

[Lemma 37 of arXiv:2603.24616, 'Pinning in non-critical half-space geometric last passage percolation'] Adopt the notation and assumptions of Theorem \ref{Thm.Tightness} and fix any $b\in (0,\beta)$. For any $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, there exist $R_1 > 0$ and $N_1\in \mathbb{N}$, depending on $b$ and $\varepsilon$, such that for all $n\ge N_1$
\begin{equation}
\begin{split}
   &\mathbb{P}\left(\max_{s\in [0, \lfloor bd_n \rfloor ]}(L_{1}^n(s) -ps) \ge R_1 d_n^{1/2}\right)  < \varepsilon.
\end{split}
\end{equation}

