[Lemma 22 of arXiv:2607.23791, 'Precise cover times for branching random walks on Hamming graphs: (iterated) logarithmic c'] On the event that no coordinate is selected by two distinct
mutation events until time $s$, we have uniformly in $y$ with zero-coordinates 
$S\subseteq\{1,\ldots,d\}$ satisfying $|S|=\ell$,
\begin{equation}
 \sum_{v\in V_s}R^{d-d_{\rm H}(X_v(s),y)}
 \ge Z_R(s)R^{\ell-2H_s\sqrt\ell}.
\end{equation}

