{"artifact_digest":"sha256:18a50c41137766d35c88120ec43996439c5ce2076a83778f538c4310b9f6eb5b","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/18/18a50c41137766d35c88120ec43996439c5ce2076a83778f538c4310b9f6eb5b.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:58447bdd7cc8dc39ddc3e4bb046c29bed942e370a1e8730112ef8cf4a7f7e870","bundle_entry_key":"2605-11451-theorem-14-strict-endpoint-chain-for-1-le","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s3_030","claim_kind":"theorem","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s3_030.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2605-11451-theorem-14-strict-endpoint-chain-for-1-le","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: Let $Z$ have density $g_p$. By Lemma~\ref{lem:normalized-gsm}, write $Z\mid V\sim N(0,V)$ with $V>0$ non-degenerate.

Conditional on independent copies $V_1,\ldots,V_k$, the normalized sum
\[
 \frac{Z_1+\cdots+Z_k}{\sqrt k}
\]
is Gaussian with variance
\[
 \overline V_k:=\frac{V_1+\cdots+V_k}{k}.
\]
Therefore
\begin{equation}
 b_{p,k}
