body:
[Lemma lem: two rare events upper bound with conditioning of arXiv:2606.13147, 'Scaling limits of the single-curve interface and outermost loops in the planar random fiel'] Let $I\subset \Lambda_{M}$ be a subset of $\Lambda_{M}.$ There exists a constant $c_9>0$ such that 
for any boundary condition $\bar\eta_I$ on $\overline{\mathrm{Ball}(I)}$ and any configuration $\xi$, we have
    \begin{equation}
\mu^{\xi,\bar\eta_I}_{\Lambda_{M}\setminus{\mathrm{Ball}(I)}}(\mathcal R)\leq c_9^{|I|}\mu^{\xi}_{\Lambda_{M}}(\mathcal R).
\end{equation}
    \begin{equation}
\mu^{\xi,\bar\eta_I}_{\Lambda_{M}\setminus{\mathrm{Ball}(I)}}(\mathcal S)\leq c_9^{|I|}\mu^{\xi}_{\Lambda_{M}}(\mathcal S).
\end{equation}
Here, notice that although $\bar\eta_I$ is an extended-Ising configuration, it naturally works as a boundary condition for the Ising measure.

