[Lemma 7 of arXiv:2606.17859, 'Full $\Gamma-$expansion for the level-two large deviation rate functionals of non-reversib'] Let $\mu\in\mss P(\bb T)$ be such that $\mu(dx) = m(x)\, dx$, where
$m\in C^2(\bb T)$ and there exists $c>0$ such that $m(x) \ge c$ for
all $x\in\bb T$.  Then,
\begin{equation*}
\ms I_\epsilon (\mu) \;=\; -\,
\int_{\bb T} \frac{\ms L_\epsilon e^H}{e^{H}} \; d\mu
\;=\; \epsilon \int_{\bb T} \mss a\,[H']^2  \; d\mu \;=\;
\frac{1 }{4\, \epsilon}\, \int_{\bb T} \mss a\,\Big\{ \, \epsilon\,
\Big[ \frac{m'}{m}
+ \frac{\mss a'}{\mss a}\Big] \,+\,  \frac{B \,/\, (\mss a\,m)} { \int_{\bb
T} 1\,/ (\mss a\, m) \,dy } \,-\, \frac{\mss b}{\mss a}  \, \Big\}^2 \, d \mu\;,
\end{equation*}
where $H$ is given by \eqref{02}.

