[Proposition 9 of arXiv:2604.07207, 'Mixing times of step-reinforced random walks'] Define a random walk $S=(S_n)_{n\in \NN}$ on $G$ by $S_0:=e_G$ and 
 \begin{equation}

      S_n := g_{L(1)}\cdot g_{L(2)}\cdots g_{L(n)}, \quad n\geq 1.
 \end{equation}
 Then $S$ is an SRRW with step distribution $\mu$ and parameter $\alpha$.

