[Proposition 26 of arXiv:2606.17452, 'Optional Stopping for Superhedging Supermartingales'] Let $(S,j)$ be an arbitrary node. Then:
\begin{enumerate}
\item If $(K_{(S,j)})$ holds then $(L_{(S,j)})$ holds.
\item $ (K_{(S,j)}) ~\mbox{holds if and only if}~ \overline{I}_j f(S) = \overline{\sigma}_j f(S)~\mbox{for any}~f \in P$.
\end{enumerate}

