body:
[Proposition 43 of arXiv:2607.07283, 'Multi-time Markov renewal chains and stratified renewal theorems'] For every $i,j\in E$ there exists a coset $a_{ij}+\mathcal L$ such that

\begin{equation*}
\psi_{ij}(k)>0\quad\Longrightarrow\quad k\in a_{ij}+\mathcal L.
\end{equation*}

Equivalently, outside the admissible coset the exact-time Markov renewal mass is zero. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 14 of arXiv:2603.28093, 'Random Stability of Random Variables'] We say that the probability generating functions $\varphi$ and $\psi$, or their corresponding distributions, or random variables $M$ and $N$, {\it commute} if 
\begin{equation}

\varphi\circ\psi \equiv \psi\circ\varphi.
\end{equation}

[Theorem 11 of arXiv:2606.26619, 'Ergodicity of stochastic reaction-diffusion equations on unbounded domains driven by space'] Under (H1)--(H3), the solution to equation (\ref{3.1}) is irreducible in $L^2_{\lambda}$, for every $\lambda>0$. More precisely, for any initial value $f\in L^2_{\lambda}$, any $T,r>0$ and $g\in L^2_{\lambda}$,
\begin{align}
  \mathbb{P}(\Vert u(T) - g\Vert_{L^2_{\lambda}}<r)>0,
\end{align}
where $u(t,x)$ is the solution to (\ref{3.1}) with initial value $f$.

