[Definition 3 of arXiv:2608.23462, '2608.23462'] Let $(y_t)_{t \in [0,\infty)}$ be a curve in $\R^{d_1}$. We say that $(y_t)_{t \in [0,\infty)}$ is an \emph{asymptotic pseudo-trajectory} of the averaged ODE \eqref{eq:averaged0} if and only if it holds 
	for all $ T \in (0,\infty) $ that
	\begin{align} 
	\lim_{T_0 \to \infty} \sup_{t \in [T_0,T_0+T]} |y_t-\mathbf x_{t-T_0}(y_{T_0})|=0.
	\end{align}

