body:
[Proposition prop:lowEstimate of arXiv:2411.14921, 'A boundary Harnack principle and its application to analyticity of 3D Brownian intersectio'] For all $u_1>1$ and $0<u_2<1$, there exists $0<C_1(u_1)<1$ such that for all $n>n_0$, $x_i\in\mathbb{R}^3$ and $|x|<1$, 
    \begin{equation*}
        \mathbb{P}_{\vec{x}}\bigg(\mathcal{W}:\mathbf{P}_{x}\Big(W[0,\tau]\cap (\mathcal{W}\setminus B(x,2^{-n}))=\varnothing\Big)\ge C_1^{nu_1^{n}}\bigg)\ge 1-u_2^{n}.
    \end{equation*}

[Definition of arXiv:2512.06640, 'Existence and sharpness of the phase transition for the frog model on transitive graphs'] We say that a graph $G$ satisfies the Poincaré Inequality if there exist $C>0$ and $C^{\prime} \geq 1$ such that for any $f \in \mathbb R^{V}$ and $r> 0:$
\begin{equation}
    \sum_{y \in B_x(r)} |f(x) - f_{r} (x)|^{2} \leq Cr^{2} \sum_{B_x(C^{\prime}r)} |\nabla f|^{2}(y) \, ,
\end{equation}
where  
\begin{equation*}
    f_{r}(x):= \frac{1}{|B_x(r)|} \sum_{y \in B_x(r)}f(y) \, .
\end{equation*}

