[Thm 8 (Aru-Lupu-Sep\'ulveda \cite{ALS1}) of arXiv:2509.01797, 'Relation between Wick powers and excursion clusters of the 2D GFF'] Let $a<v$. Fix $z\in D$.
Then the r.v. 
\begin{displaymath}
\dfrac{1}{2\pi}\log\Big(\dfrac{\CR(z,D)}{\CR(z,D\setminus A_{a})}\Big)
\end{displaymath}
has the same distribution as $T_a$ under $W_0 = v$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Proposition 24 (Cyclotomic-local knot germ) of arXiv:2608.29585, '2608.29585'] Fix a zero-framed knot $K$ and an integer $n\ge2$.  For every $d\ge1$
and $s\in\Z$, the series
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr J_{K,s}(z)=
 \sum_{k\ge0}b_k^{(n)}(K;q)U_k(z)
\end{equation}
converges in $\mathscr A_{d,s}$.  If $i\in\Z_{\ge0}$ and
$z_i\equiv z_s\pmod{\pi_d}$, then continuous evaluation at
$u_s=z_i-z_s$ gives
\begin{equation}
 \mathscr J_{K,s}(z_i)=J_i^{SU(n)}(K;q).
\end{equation}

