    with $q(t,s) = 1-s+\max((s-1)^+,t) = (1+t-s)^+$ and $k(t,s) = \Ind_{\{s < t+1\}}$. Therefore, $0 \leq q(t,s) \leq 1$ for all $t,s \in [0,T]$ with $s \geq t$.
    Now by Theorem \ref{thm:existence-of-noncontinuable-riccati} there exists a unique noncontinuable solution $(\psi,T_{\text{min}})$ to equation
    \eqref{eq:riccati-pd-vol}. Let $\psi^r$ and $\psi^i$ denote the real and imaginary parts of $\psi$. ...","release_manifest_digest":"sha256:60ff49911744355acad156b3e63af3212d91891475a6d7ae2c1bfc28bd9a31a0","revision_digest":"sha256:ba6aca8f8c2e20da7da88bb96bb224cd6b7f20083782fe10dbcc355d2eb90d69","source_id":"arxiv:2606.23099","source_revision":"tex-as-downloaded-2026-09-07","statement_fidelity_reviewed":false,"supersedes":[],"trust_class":"curated_secondary","truth_status":"unverified"}

