[Proposition property of LN of arXiv:2606.01944, 'Propagation of Chaos for Mean-field Mean Reflected Backward Stochastic Differential Equati'] (i) For any $X,Y\in L^2(\mathcal{F}^{(N)}_t;\mathbb{R}^N)$, we have 
    \begin{align}
        |L_t^{(N)}(X)-L_t^{(N)}(Y)|\le \frac{M}{m}\frac{1}{N}\sum_{j=1}^N|X^j-Y^j|.
    \end{align}

  \noindent  (ii) For any $S\in\mathcal{S}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)};\mathbb{R}^N)$, we have $\{L^{(N)}_t(S_t)\}_{t\in[0,T]}\in \mathcal{S}^2(\mathbb{F}^{(N)})$.

