[Lemma 12 of arXiv:2604.07207, 'Mixing times of step-reinforced random walks'] For $n\geq 1$, one has
  \begin{equation}

y_n=\beta_n \left(y_1+\sum_{j=1}^{n-1} \frac{\gamma_j}{\beta_{j+1}} \epsilon_{j+1}\right),
  \end{equation}
where $(\varepsilon_{j+1})_{j\geq 1}$  defined by
\begin{equation}

    \varepsilon_{j+1}:= \frac{1}{1+\alpha} \left(I(j+1)-I(j)- (1-\alpha) + \frac{\alpha I(j)}{j}\right), \quad j\geq 1,
\end{equation}
is a martingale difference sequence with respect to $(\F_{j+1})_{j\geq 1}$.

