[Definition def:finiteLE of arXiv:2608.05089, 'Correlation decay in area-tilted line ensembles'] For any $\lambda > 0$, let $\mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\lambda}_{n,\ell,r}$ denote the probability distribution
on functions $\mathbf{X}_n=(X^1_n,X^2_n,\ldots, X^n_n) : [\ell,r] \to \mathbb{A}_+^n$ defined by the Radon--Nikodym derivative
\begin{equation}
    \frac{d \mathcal{L}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y},\lambda}_{n,\ell,r}}{d \mathcal{B}^{\mathbf{x},\mathbf{y}}_{n,\ell,r}}(\mathbf{X}_n)
    \propto \Exp{-2 \sum_{i=1}^n \lambda^{i-1} \int_\ell^r X^i_n(t) \,dt}
    \ind{\mathbf{X}_n(t) \in \mathbb{A}_+^n \text{ for all } t \in [\ell,r]}.
\end{equation}

