Differentiating (equation eq:FP-kernel-formula of the paper) by
$\partial_{a_p}$ produces boundary contributions from the
lower limits $a_i$ and $a_j$ via the Leibniz rule, and
interior contributions where $\partial_{a_p}$ acts on $B$
through the splitting identity (equation eq:FP-splitting of the paper).
All terms carry a minus sign (from
$\partial_{a_p}\int_{a_p}^{\infty} f = -f(a_p)$ and
from the sign in (equation eq:FP-splitting of the paper)):
\begin{align*}
\partial_{a_p} K
&= -\psi_{x_p,a_p}\phi_{x_p,a_p}
