\end{itemize}
In all other cases, leave the configuration unchanged. 
\item[(2)] Assume that  $U> (1+q)^{-1}$. If $\{ \xi^{\modi}_{t_-}(x), \xi^{\modi}_{t_-}(x+1) \}  \neq \{\Aup,\Bup\}$, then sort the endpoints in $\xi^{\modi}_t$ with respect to  \eqref{def:ExtendedPartialOrder} in decreasing order. If $\{ \xi^{\modi}_{t_-}(x), \xi^{\modi}_{t_-}(x+1) \}  = \{\Aup,\Bup\}$, then set $\xi^{\modi}_t(x)=\onep$ and $\xi^{\modi}_t(x+1)=\zerop$. Moreover, for all $y=x \mod N$ with $y \neq x$, we distinguish the following four sub-cases:
