[Cor lambda_conv of arXiv:2509.08659, 'Gap metrics for stationary point processes and quantitative convexity of the free energy'] Let $1<p<2$  and let  $\mathsf{P}_i\in  \mathcal P_{s,1}(\Gamma)$, $i=0,1$ with  finite free energy $\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_i)<\infty$, and $\Pi_i:= \mathsf{gap}(\mathsf{P}_i)$ for  $i=0,1$. Assume that the function $f^{p/(p-2)}$  (cf. assumption (assumption1 of the paper)) is convex on $[0,\infty)$ and  $\int f^{p/(p-2)}( \mathsf{s}_1)\Pi_i(d \mathsf{s})<\infty$ for $i=0,1$. Then $ \mathscr W_p(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)<\infty$ and 
     \begin{align*}
     \mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{t})&\leq (1-t)\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{0})+t\mathcal F_{\beta}(\mathsf{P}_{1})\\
     &-\frac{\beta(1-t)t}{2} \mathscr W_p^2(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)\left[ \max\left(\int f^{p/(p-2)}( \mathsf{s}_1)\Pi_0(d \mathsf{s}),\int f^{p/(p-2)}( \mathsf{s}_1)\Pi_1(d \mathsf{s})\right)\right]^{\frac{p-2}{p}},
\end{align*}
 where  $ \mathsf{Q}\in  \mathsf{Cpl}_{s,m}(\mathsf{P}_0,\mathsf{P}_1)$ is the $\mathscr W_p-$optimal coupling from  Theorem (thm:interaction_gain of the paper), $\mathsf U:=\iota( \mathsf{Q})$ and  $\mathsf{P}_t:= \mathsf{gap}^{-1}\left((T_t)_{\#}\mathsf U\right)$.

