{"artifact_digest":"sha256:281507c6a5d6931f58ccee7a966a78ed2f9d90e28418642a5449d1b4604f8e15","artifact_path":"objects/sha256/28/281507c6a5d6931f58ccee7a966a78ed2f9d90e28418642a5449d1b4604f8e15.md","bundle_digest":"sha256:d95f0f16087b248dd076c1e2a2ffb59c787aaca624a44a2efbe860121516ac0b","bundle_entry_key":"2507-08909-lemma-84-h0-sing-only","bundle_id":"population.tex-extract-s0_006","claim_kind":"lemma","conditions":[],"domain":"probability theory","draft":"tex-extract-20260907/bundle_s0_006.json","evidence_ids":[],"logical_id":"math:harvest.arxiv.mathematics:arxiv-2507-08909-lem-84-h0-sing-only","overlay_schema_version":1,"proof_text":"Paper's own proof, opening: \emph{Part (a).}\quad For this $\phi$ and $O$, Corollary~\ref{cor:APent-properties-trace}(a) gives an integer $d_0$ and a neighbourhood $V$ of $\tau$ such that
