[Lemma HOProb of arXiv:2511.15893, 'On a Class of Dynamical Poisson-Voronoi Tessellations'] Suppose $h_1, h_2\in \mathbb{R}^+$ and $t_1, t_2\in \mathbb{R}$ such that $t_2\leq t_1$, for $h_1<h_2$ and $t_2\leq t_1-t^*$, for $h_1>h_2$, where $t^*$ is defined in ((eq:tstar of the paper)). Under the two-point Palm probability measure $\mathbb{P}^{(t_1, h_1), (t_2,h_2)}_{{\mathcal H }}$, the probability of the event $A^{(k)}_{2,1}$,  for $k=1,2$, is 

\begin{align}\mathbb{E}_{{\mathcal H }}\left[{\mathds{1}}_{A^{(k)}_{2,1}}\left({\mathcal H }^1+\delta_{(t_1, h_1)}+{\mathcal H }^2+\delta_{(t_2, h_2)}\right)\right]&=e^{-\lambda\pi\hat h^2_k},{\nonumber}
\end{align}

where $\hat h_k$ is determined in ((eq:HO_distance1 of the paper)) as a function of $t_1-t_2, h_1, h_2$. (Proof in the paper; no proof environment follows the statement in the TeX.)

[Definition 1 (Terminal atomic mass) of arXiv:2608.30715, 'Endpoint Energy Atoms Force Local Pressure Concentration in Three-Dimensional Navier--Stok'] For an \(L^2\)-bounded field \(q(t)\), a point \(a\in\Omega\), and a terminal
time \(T_*\), define
\begin{equation}
 \Aa_a[q]
