[Definition def:grafting of arXiv:2411.07157, 'Rough differential equations in the flow approach'] Given $\underline{\tau}_1, \underline{\tau}_2\in \boldsymbol{\mathfrak{T}}$, we define, for any $n \in N(\underline{\tau}_1)$ a new labelled tree $\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_1 \in \boldsymbol{\mathfrak{T}}$ which will be constructed by ``grafting the tree $\underline{\tau}_2$ onto $\underline{\tau}_1$ at the node $n$''. More precisely, we set 
\begin{equs}  
r(\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_1 )\eqdef r(\underline{\tau}_1)\,,\; 
\enskip 
N(\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_1 ) \eqdef N(\underline{\tau}_1) \cup {N}\big(\underline{\tau}_2+ \ell_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2} \big)\,,
\end{equs}
and
\begin{equs}   
{E}(\underline{\tau}_2 \graft_{n} \underline{\tau}_1) \eqdef E(\underline{\tau}_1) \cup E\big(\underline{\tau}_2+ \ell_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2} \big) \cup \big\{\{{r}\big(\underline{\tau}_2+ \ell_{\underline{\tau}_1,\underline{\tau}_2} 
 \big),n\}\big\}\,.
\end{equs}

[Theorem 5 (Statistical guarantees for the Gibbs posterior) of arXiv:2608.25706, 'Fast rates in Bayesian online learning with approximate posteriors'] Under \cref{ass:design,ass:linear-loss,ass:stationarity,ass:prior}, the exact Gibbs posterior satisfies
    \begin{equation}
    \E\sbr{\W^2(\Pi_t,\delta_{\theta^\star})}\lesssim t^{-1}
    \end{equation}
and
