[Lemma 69 of arXiv:2607.10486, 'Weak martingale solutions to stochastic Navier-Stokes-Cahn-Hilliard system with transport '] Assume that $\bu \in L^2(0,T;\StokesH)$ and $(\bu_n)_{n \in \mathbb{N}}$ is a bounded sequence in $L^2(0,T;\StokesH)$ such that
$\bu_n \to \bu$ in $L^2(0,T;\StokesH)$. Then, for every $z_1 \in \rU_0$,
  \begin{equation}
    \lim_{n \to \infty} \int_0^T \lvert \duality{\bB_{0,n}(\bu_n(s),\bu_n(s)) - \bB_0(\bu(s),\bu(s))}{z_1}{\rU_0}{\rU_0^\prime} \rvert\,\d s=0.
  \end{equation}

